f=\"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiggFBVV95cUxNNG9CU1d0QnJYQkJvZ0ZTTFRTR29wclhYeUJhejBUejJReHVoa3pqTlRDTXFyRFdld3F3NFlpV3Bxa01NaWh2d21kVGFGam9CNUlLRUFKb2QyUzBtZ1Vlc2NocGFJTFBhZkxXTnZiTDc3Q2N0N3cyTHcxTEQydllGR3RB?oc=5\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;“新时代·发现中国”｜国际智库媒体专家走读西安，触摸丝路新脉动&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font color=\"#6f6f6f\"&gt;新华网&lt;/font&gt;</description><source url=\"http://www.sn.xinhuanet.com\">新华网</source></item></channel></rss>","fetchedAt":"2026-11-15T12:59:39.015Z"},"mercopress":{"xml":"\r\n<rss version=\"2.0\" xmlns:atom=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom\">\r\n\r\n<channel>\r\n  <title>MercoPress</title>\r\n  <link>https://en.mercopress.com/</link>\r\n  <atom:link  rel=\"self\" type=\"application/rss+xml\" href=\"https://en.mercopress.com/rss/\" />\r\n  <description>South Atlantic News Agency</description>\r\n  <language>en</language>\r\n    <copyright>Copyright 2026, MercoPress.</copyright>\r\n  <image>\r\n    <url>https://en.mercopress.com/web/img/en/mercopress-logo.gif</url>\r\n    <title>MercoPress</title>\r\n    <link>http://en.mercopress.com/</link>\r\n  </image>  \r\n    <item>\r\n      <title><![CDATA[US resumes flights after a four-and-a-half-hour shutdown caused by obsolete equipment]]></title>\r\n      <link><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/14/us-resumes-flights-after-a-four-and-a-half-hour-shutdown-caused-by-obsolete-equipment?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></link>\r\n      <guid><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/14/us-resumes-flights-after-a-four-and-a-half-hour-shutdown-caused-by-obsolete-equipment?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></guid>\r\n      <description><![CDATA[<p>\r\n\t   \t      <img src=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112106/100x80/asd4g4.jpg\" alt=\"Photo: AP / Ross Franklin\" width=\"100\" height=\"80\" style=\"float:left;margin:0 12px 6px 0;border:1px solid #333\" />\r\n\t         The US Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) on Friday night lifted the nationwide ground stop it had ordered in the afternoon, after some four and a half hours of airspace closure that left thousands of flights cancelled. Donald Trump’s administration blamed the failure on overloaded, outdated analogue telecommunications equipment at air traffic control centres, ruled out a cyberattack for now and warned that the return to normal would be slow.</p>]]></description>\r\n      <enclosure url=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112106/100x80/asd4g4.jpg\" length=\"0\" type=\"image/jpg\" />      <category><![CDATA[Politics, Tourism, United States]]></category>\r\n      <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:24:00 GMT</pubDate>\r\n    </item>    \r\n    <item>\r\n      <title><![CDATA[US grounds all departing flights over an air traffic control communications failure]]></title>\r\n      <link><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/14/us-grounds-all-departing-flights-over-an-air-traffic-control-communications-failure?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></link>\r\n      <guid><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/14/us-grounds-all-departing-flights-over-an-air-traffic-control-communications-failure?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></guid>\r\n      <description><![CDATA[<p>\r\n\t   \t      <img src=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112101/100x80/usflig.jpg\" alt=\"Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said the failure affects the 22 regional centres that guide aircraft en route between airports and that FAA technicians are investigating\" width=\"100\" height=\"80\" style=\"float:left;margin:0 12px 6px 0;border:1px solid #333\" />\r\n\t         The US Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) on Friday ordered a halt to all flights departing from the country’s airports “due to extraordinary circumstances and for reasons of safety”, following a communications failure affecting air traffic control centres. Thousands of flights were cancelled or delayed and hundreds of thousands of passengers were stranded. The government has so far ruled out an attack.</p>]]></description>\r\n      <enclosure url=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112101/100x80/usflig.jpg\" length=\"0\" type=\"image/jpg\" />      <category><![CDATA[Tourism, United States]]></category>\r\n      <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:53:00 GMT</pubDate>\r\n    </item>    \r\n    <item>\r\n      <title><![CDATA[Microsoft restores services after a global outage hit Outlook and Teams in more than 70 countries]]></title>\r\n      <link><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/13/microsoft-restores-services-after-a-global-outage-hit-outlook-and-teams-in-more-than-70-countries?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></link>\r\n      <guid><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/13/microsoft-restores-services-after-a-global-outage-hit-outlook-and-teams-in-more-than-70-countries?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></guid>\r\n      <description><![CDATA[<p>\r\n\t   \t      <img src=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112099/100x80/micro.jpg\" alt=\"In Australia, the outage affected the tax office, some courts, the Federal Police, the ASIO intelligence agency and the New South Wales state services platform\" width=\"100\" height=\"80\" style=\"float:left;margin:0 12px 6px 0;border:1px solid #333\" />\r\n\t         Microsoft said on Friday its services were recovering after a global outage that began on Thursday afternoon, European time, and for hours affected millions of users in more than 70 countries, including public bodies in Australia and Japan. The company ruled out a cyberattack.</p>]]></description>\r\n      <enclosure url=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112099/100x80/micro.jpg\" length=\"0\" type=\"image/jpg\" />      <category><![CDATA[International]]></category>\r\n      <pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:09:00 GMT</pubDate>\r\n    </item>    \r\n    <item>\r\n      <title><![CDATA[Chile tells Argentina “countries do not ask permission” for its ship bound for the Falklands]]></title>\r\n      <link><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/13/chile-tells-argentina-countries-do-not-ask-permission-for-its-ship-bound-for-the-falklands?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></link>\r\n      <guid><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/13/chile-tells-argentina-countries-do-not-ask-permission-for-its-ship-bound-for-the-falklands?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></guid>\r\n      <description><![CDATA[<p>\r\n\t   \t      <img src=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112097/100x80/chi.jpg\" alt=\"The Chilean-flagged Danstar aims to restore a route suspended for some 15 years, carrying food, machinery and building materials as an alternative to supplies from Montevideo\" width=\"100\" height=\"80\" style=\"float:left;margin:0 12px 6px 0;border:1px solid #333\" />\r\n\t         Chile’s Foreign Minister Francisco Pérez Mackenna has ruled out asking Argentina for authorisation for the voyage of the Chilean vessel Danstar, which plans to reopen the commercial route between Punta Arenas and the Falklands in December, invoking the right of innocent passage recognised by the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea. “Countries do not ask permission,” he said, according to Argentina’s La Nación.</p>]]></description>\r\n      <enclosure url=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112097/100x80/chi.jpg\" length=\"0\" type=\"image/jpg\" />      <category><![CDATA[Politics, Argentina, Falkland Islands, Chile]]></category>\r\n      <pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:06:00 GMT</pubDate>\r\n    </item>    \r\n    <item>\r\n      <title><![CDATA[Leo XIV to 52,000 young people in Lima: “Be passionate about everything worthwhile”]]></title>\r\n      <link><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/13/leo-xiv-to-52-000-young-people-in-lima-be-passionate-about-everything-worthwhile?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></link>\r\n      <guid><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/13/leo-xiv-to-52-000-young-people-in-lima-be-passionate-about-everything-worthwhile?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></guid>\r\n      <description><![CDATA[<p>\r\n\t   \t      <img src=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112092/100x80/2papa.jpg\" alt=\"Photo: REUTERS/Yara Nardi\" width=\"100\" height=\"80\" style=\"float:left;margin:0 12px 6px 0;border:1px solid #333\" />\r\n\t         Pope Leo XIV met some 52,000 young people at Lima’s National Stadium on Thursday, according to El País, in the last event of his stay in the Peruvian capital before travelling to Chiclayo, the diocese he led as bishop. “Someone told me that Peru needs hope. You are the sign of hope,” he told them, to applause.</p>]]></description>\r\n      <enclosure url=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112092/100x80/2papa.jpg\" length=\"0\" type=\"image/jpg\" />      <category><![CDATA[Politics, International, Latin America]]></category>\r\n      <pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:58:00 GMT</pubDate>\r\n    </item>    \r\n    <item>\r\n      <title><![CDATA[British veteran returns to an Argentine veteran the helmet he took in 1982]]></title>\r\n      <link><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/12/british-veteran-returns-to-an-argentine-veteran-the-helmet-he-took-in-1982?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></link>\r\n      <guid><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/12/british-veteran-returns-to-an-argentine-veteran-the-helmet-he-took-in-1982?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></guid>\r\n      <description><![CDATA[<p>\r\n\t   \t      <img src=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112090/100x80/gart.jpeg\" alt=\"Aged 18, Andy Gatrick found two wounded Argentine soldiers, later captured, at Mount Harriet in June 1982 and kept one&rsquo;s helmet, which bore a name: Hector. Photo: Mick Dawson\" width=\"100\" height=\"80\" style=\"float:left;margin:0 12px 6px 0;border:1px solid #333\" />\r\n\t         A former Royal Marine has travelled to Argentina to return to an Argentine veteran the helmet he took during the Battle of Mount Harriet in the 1982 Falklands War, in a reunion filmed for a documentary, BBC Sussex reported.</p>]]></description>\r\n      <enclosure url=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112090/100x80/gart.jpeg\" length=\"0\" type=\"image/jpg\" />      <category><![CDATA[Politics, Argentina, Falkland Islands, International]]></category>\r\n      <pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:01:00 GMT</pubDate>\r\n    </item>    \r\n    <item>\r\n      <title><![CDATA[Lula to visit Madrid on Monday to meet Sánchez, two weeks before Spain’s election]]></title>\r\n      <link><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/12/lula-to-visit-madrid-on-monday-to-meet-sanchez-two-weeks-before-spain-s-election?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></link>\r\n      <guid><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/12/lula-to-visit-madrid-on-monday-to-meet-sanchez-two-weeks-before-spain-s-election?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></guid>\r\n      <description><![CDATA[<p>\r\n\t   \t      <img src=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112088/100x80/espbra.jpg\" alt=\"The visit will also include a political event at which Lula will expressly back the Socialist candidate, and S&aacute;nchez&rsquo;s team had spent two weeks trying to arrange it\" width=\"100\" height=\"80\" style=\"float:left;margin:0 12px 6px 0;border:1px solid #333\" />\r\n\t         Brazilian President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva will visit Madrid on Monday, November 16, to meet Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez, less than two weeks before the snap general election on November 29, in which Sánchez is seeking re-election. It will be Lula’s first visit to Spain since he won Brazil’s election on October 25.</p>]]></description>\r\n      <enclosure url=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112088/100x80/espbra.jpg\" length=\"0\" type=\"image/jpg\" />      <category><![CDATA[Politics, Brazil, International]]></category>\r\n      <pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:02:00 GMT</pubDate>\r\n    </item>    \r\n    <item>\r\n      <title><![CDATA[Paraguay’s banking superintendent arrested in the Ueno Bank investigation]]></title>\r\n      <link><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/12/paraguay-s-banking-superintendent-arrested-in-the-ueno-bank-investigation?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></link>\r\n      <guid><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/12/paraguay-s-banking-superintendent-arrested-in-the-ueno-bank-investigation?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></guid>\r\n      <description><![CDATA[<p>\r\n\t   \t      <img src=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112085/100x80/holger-insfra-n.jpg\" alt=\"Insfr&aacute;n was named in a criminal complaint expanded by opposition lawmakers last week, alongside the economy minister and other officials\" width=\"100\" height=\"80\" style=\"float:left;margin:0 12px 6px 0;border:1px solid #333\" />\r\n\t         Paraguay’s Superintendent of Banks, Holger Insfrán, was arrested on Thursday as part of the investigation into the collapse of Ueno Bank, which has already led to the pre-trial detention of former President Santiago Peña and former Central Bank president Carlos Carvallo, according to prosecution sources cited by the EFE news agency. The charges against him have not been disclosed.</p>]]></description>\r\n      <enclosure url=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112085/100x80/holger-insfra-n.jpg\" length=\"0\" type=\"image/jpg\" />      <category><![CDATA[Economy, Politics, Paraguay]]></category>\r\n      <pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:20:00 GMT</pubDate>\r\n    </item>    \r\n    <item>\r\n      <title><![CDATA[Leo XIV arrives in Peru, his “homeland”, defending international law and reconciliation]]></title>\r\n      <link><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/12/leo-xiv-arrives-in-peru-his-homeland-defending-international-law-and-reconciliation?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></link>\r\n      <guid><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/12/leo-xiv-arrives-in-peru-his-homeland-defending-international-law-and-reconciliation?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></guid>\r\n      <description><![CDATA[<p>\r\n\t   \t      <img src=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112082/100x80/papa.jpg\" alt=\"Leo XIV will remain in Peru until Monday, November 16. On Friday he will celebrate Mass in Pimentel, near Chiclayo, the diocese he led from 2015 to 2023\" width=\"100\" height=\"80\" style=\"float:left;margin:0 12px 6px 0;border:1px solid #333\" />\r\n\t         Pope Leo XIV arrived in Lima on Wednesday, the final stage of his South American tour, and in his first speech in Peru, the country where he lived for some twenty years and whose nationality he holds, called for diplomacy that “respects international law” in the face of wars and for the country’s past events “to be dealt with justice and sensitivity”.</p>]]></description>\r\n      <enclosure url=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112082/100x80/papa.jpg\" length=\"0\" type=\"image/jpg\" />      <category><![CDATA[Politics, International, Latin America]]></category>\r\n      <pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:59:00 GMT</pubDate>\r\n    </item>    \r\n    <item>\r\n      <title><![CDATA[Law of the sea tribunal to rule on November 28 on Argentina’s bid to halt Sea Lion]]></title>\r\n      <link><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/12/law-of-the-sea-tribunal-to-rule-on-november-28-on-argentina-s-bid-to-halt-sea-lion?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></link>\r\n      <guid><![CDATA[https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/12/law-of-the-sea-tribunal-to-rule-on-november-28-on-argentina-s-bid-to-halt-sea-lion?utm_source=feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_content=main&utm_campaign=rss]]></guid>\r\n      <description><![CDATA[<p>\r\n\t   \t      <img src=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112078/100x80/itlos.jpg\" alt=\"Because the United Kingdom chose the International Court of Justice and Argentina the Hamburg tribunal, the merits of the case will be decided by an arbitral tribunal\" width=\"100\" height=\"80\" style=\"float:left;margin:0 12px 6px 0;border:1px solid #333\" />\r\n\t         The International Tribunal for the Law of the Sea will announce on Saturday, November 28, its decision on Argentina’s request for provisional measures to halt the Sea Lion oil project north of the Falklands, after two days of hearings concluded in Hamburg on Wednesday. Argentina presented final requests that were more specific than its initial ones, and the United Kingdom asked the tribunal to reject them all.</p>]]></description>\r\n      <enclosure url=\"https://en.mercopress.com/data/cache/noticias/112078/100x80/itlos.jpg\" length=\"0\" type=\"image/jpg\" />      <category><![CDATA[Politics, Argentina, Falkland Islands, International]]></category>\r\n      <pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:58:00 GMT</pubDate>\r\n    </item>    \r\n\r\n  </channel>\r\n</rss>\r\n","fetchedAt":"2026-11-15T12:59:07.864Z"},"reuters":{"xml":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\" standalone=\"yes\"?><rss version=\"2.0\" xmlns:media=\"http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/\"><channel><generator>NFE/5.0</generator><title>\"when:24h site:reuters.com\" - Google News</title><link>https://news.google.com/search?q=when:24h+site:reuters.com&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US:en</link><language>en-US</language><webMaster>news-webmaster@google.com</webMaster><copyright>Copyright © 2026 Google. All rights reserved. This XML feed is made available solely for the purpose of ren