 height=\"135\" credit=\"ABCNews.com\" /><media:thumbnail url=\"https://s.abcnews.com/images/GMA/261113_gma_katersky_esb1_0735_hpMain_4x3_608.jpg\" width=\"608\" height=\"456\" credit=\"ABCNews.com\" /><media:thumbnail url=\"https://s.abcnews.com/images/GMA/261113_gma_katersky_esb1_0735_hpMain_16x9_992.jpg\" width=\"992\" height=\"558\" credit=\"ABCNews.com\" /><media:thumbnail url=\"https://s.abcnews.com/images/GMA/261113_gma_katersky_esb1_0735_hpMain_16x9_1600.jpg\" width=\"1600\" height=\"900\" credit=\"ABCNews.com\" />\n\t\t\t<media:keywords>10</media:keywords>\n\t\t\t<title><![CDATA[WATCH:  Empire State Building climbers appear in court]]></title>\n\t\t\t<link><![CDATA[https://abcnews.com/video/138104770/]]></link>\n\t\t\t<guid><![CDATA[https://abcnews.com/video/138104770/]]></guid>\n\t\t\t<pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:13:51 -0500</pubDate>\n\t\t\t<description><![CDATA[The daredevil couple who were arrested after climbing to the top of the Empire State Building were in court on Thursday to face criminal charges and possible deportation.]]></description>\n\t\t\t<category>GMA</category>\n\t\t\t</item><item><media:thumbnail url=\"https://s.abcnews.com/images/WNT/261112_wn_tanker_truck_hpMain_4x3_384.jpg\" width=\"384\" height=\"288\" credit=\"ABCNews.com\" /><media:thumbnail url=\"https://s.abcnews.com/images/WNT/261112_wn_tanker_truck_hpMain_4x3_144.jpg\" width=\"144\" height=\"108\" credit=\"ABCNews.com\" /><media:thumbnail url=\"https://s.abcnews.com/images/WNT/261112_wn_tanker_truck_hpMain_4x3_384.jpg\" width=\"384\" height=\"288\" credit=\"ABCNews.com\" /><media:thumbnail url=\"https://s.abcnews.com/images/WNT/261112_wn_tanker_truck_hpMain_16x9_240.jpg\" width=\"240\" height=\"135\" credit=\"ABCNews.com\" /><media:thumbnail url=\"https://s.abcnews.com/images/WNT/261112_wn_tanker_truck_hpMain_4x3_608.jpg\" width=\"608\" height=\"456\" credit=\"ABCNews.com\" /><media:thumbnail url=\"https://s.abcnews.com/images/WNT/261112_wn_tanker_truck_hpMain_16x9_992.jpg\" wi