ipwFBVV95cUxPRjFiQXFycEFSQlJHMVc5ZlhLckk5TWlrc0txQW1HMlEwTUktSTVOUkt4c0IyZzdJMEJvSmF6TTFKRkpuOHZjWVhLbHhSdG01SERKYWdET1ZsS2VtMjltTnhQRVdBY1VRYXEzMXh5ZHhjOHN0Vkwwc1hiZVdVMU1DbVBQeUtZX1l3Nks2Qm5YbHB1ZGN0ck1ZdnRtd0FwYzNwOXkwU1F4WQ</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:23:00 GMT</pubDate><description>&lt;a href=\"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipwFBVV95cUxPRjFiQXFycEFSQlJHMVc5ZlhLckk5TWlrc0txQW1HMlEwTUktSTVOUkt4c0IyZzdJMEJvSmF6TTFKRkpuOHZjWVhLbHhSdG01SERKYWdET1ZsS2VtMjltTnhQRVdBY1VRYXEzMXh5ZHhjOHN0Vkwwc1hiZVdVMU1DbVBQeUtZX1l3Nks2Qm5YbHB1ZGN0ck1ZdnRtd0FwYzNwOXkwU1F4WQ?oc=5\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;Officers resuscitate infant who stopped breathing&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font color=\"#6f6f6f\"&gt;WDBJ7&lt;/font&gt;</description><source url=\"https://www.wdbj7.com\">WDBJ7</source></item></channel></rss>","fetchedAt":"2026-11-15T12:59:39.015Z"},"bloomberg":{"xml":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?><rss xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xmlns:content=\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\" xmlns:atom=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom\" version=\"2.0\" xmlns:media=\"http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/\">\n    <channel>\n        <title><![CDATA[Bloomberg Politics]]></title>\n        <description><![CDATA[Bloomberg.com.]]></description>\n        <link>http://bloomberg.com/politics/</link>\n        <image>\n            <url>http://www.bloomberg.com/feeds/static/images/bloomberg_logo_blue.png</url>\n            <title>Bloomberg Politics</title>\n            <link>http://bloomberg.com/politics/</link>\n        </image>\n        <generator>RSS for Node</generator>\n        <lastBuildDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:57:23 GMT</lastBuildDate>\n        <atom:link href=\"https://www.bloomberg.com/feeds/politics/news.rss\" rel=\"self\" type=\"application/rss+xml\"/>\n        <copyright><![CDATA[Copyright 2026 BLOOMBERG L.P. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED]]></copyright>\n        <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>\n        <item>\n            <title><![CDATA[Burnham Faces Labour Rebellion Over Rosebank, Sunday Times Says]]></title>\n            <description><![CDATA[A group of Labour lawmakers is attempting to block approval for drilling at the Rosebank oil field, presenting UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham with the first major rebellion of his premiership, the Sunday Times reported.]]></description>\n            <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-15/burnham-faces-labour-rebellion-over-rosebank-sunday-times-says</link>\n            <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">TOJFFLKJH6V400</guid>\n            <dc:creator><![CDATA[Marcus Wright]]></dc:creator>\n            <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:14:23 GMT</pubDate>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <title><![CDATA[Hungary Opens Pandora’s Box With Publication of Communist Files]]></title>\n            <description><![CDATA[<p>Peter Magyar’s quest to “heal” the country is tougher than he thought.</p>]]></description>\n            <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-15/hungary-opens-pandora-s-box-with-publication-of-communist-files</link>\n            <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">TOJEE4N3N08Y00</guid>\n            <dc:creator><![CDATA[Zoltan Simon]]></dc:creator>\n            <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:30:04 GMT</pubDate>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <title><![CDATA[Malay Parties Sweep Latest Regional Vote in Blow to Anwar]]></title>\n            <description><![CDATA[An alliance of Malaysia’s two largest ethnic-Malay parties swept the country’s latest regional vote, dealing Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim’s coalition its third straight electoral setback this year.]]></description>\n            <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-15/anwar-s-coalition-suffers-third-straight-regional-poll-defeat</link>\n            <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">TOF1SGKJH6VO00</guid>\n            <dc:creator><![CDATA[Danial Azhar]]></dc:creator>\n            <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:45:48 GMT</pubDate>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <title><![CDATA[Zelenskyy Says US Floats NATO Deal as Kushner Leans on Europe]]></title>\n            <description><![CDATA[Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said US peace envoys asked whether Ukraine would be willing to cede the Donbas region to Russia in exchange for NATO membership, signaling a potential shift in Washington’s negotiating tactics, as a top US envoy called for “direct engagement” between Europe and Moscow.]]></description>\n            <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-14/zelenskyy-says-us-floats-nato-for-ukraine-in-exchange-for-donbas</link>\n            <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">TOGGLXR24U8A00</guid>\n            <dc:creator><![CDATA[Volodymyr Verbianyi]]></dc:creator>\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:32:42 GMT</pubDate>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <title><![CDATA[Iran Strikes Bahrain Base, Repeats Path to US Deal Remains Open]]></title>\n            <description><![CDATA[Iran targeted an air base in Bahrain in the first direct strike on the Gulf state in weeks, even as it reiterated that a path to ending the conflict with the US remains open.]]></description>\n            <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-15/iran-strikes-bahrain-base-repeats-path-to-us-deal-remains-open</link>\n            <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">TOJ8JJKGIFPE00</guid>\n            <dc:creator><![CDATA[Arsalan Shahla and Sara Gharaibeh]]></dc:creator>\n            <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:14:04 GMT</pubDate>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <title><![CDATA[Australia, Philippines Upgrade Defense Ties With Focus on China]]></title>\n            <description><![CDATA[Australia and the Philippines signed a new defense pact Sunday, boosting military cooperation as the US allies face a more assertive China in the Asia-Pacific region.]]></description>\n            <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-15/australia-philippines-upgrade-defense-ties-with-focus-on-china</link>\n            <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">TOIUF2T9NJLS00</guid>\n            <dc:creator><![CDATA[James Mayger and Cliff Venzon]]></dc:creator>\n            <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:29:19 GMT</pubDate>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <title><![CDATA[Trump’s White House Lawyer on Subpoena Compliance: ‘It Depends’]]></title>\n            <description><![CDATA[The White House won’t commit to complying with potential subpoenas from a Democratic-led Congress and believes company executives who’ve had contact with President Donald Trump may be covered by executive privilege, White House Counsel Will Scharf said.]]></description>\n            <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-14/trump-s-white-house-lawyer-on-subpoena-compliance-it-depends</link>\n            <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">TOGUL4KJH6V400</guid>\n            <dc:creator><![CDATA[Jeff Mason]]></dc:creator>\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:04:15 GMT</pubDate>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <title><![CDATA[Kushner Wants Direct Russia-Europe Talks in Ukraine Peace Push]]></title>\n            <description><![CDATA[Jared Kushner, the US president’s son-in-law who has been serving as a negotiator with Russia and Ukraine, said the Trump administration wants to see direct talks between Moscow and US allies in Europe.]]></description>\n            <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-14/kushner-wants-direct-russia-europe-talks-in-ukraine-peace-push</link>\n            <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">TOIEWVT96OSG00</guid>\n            <dc:creator><![CDATA[Kevin Whitelaw]]></dc:creator>\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:47:26 GMT</pubDate>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <title><![CDATA[Flush With Wins, Democrats Confront Fear of Fleeting Success]]></title>\n            <description><![CDATA[Democrats gathered this week to celebrate their biggest electoral triumph in a generation and confront an inescapable anxiety — the risk of squandering it all.]]></description>\n            <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-14/flush-with-wins-democrats-confront-fear-of-fleeting-success</link>\n            <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">TOF8EAKGIFQP00</guid>\n            <dc:creator><![CDATA[Josh Wingrove]]></dc:creator>\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:22:50 GMT</pubDate>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <title><![CDATA[Pentagon Eyes Smaller Troop Cuts Across Europe in Reversal]]></title>\n            <description><![CDATA[The Trump administration’s cuts to roughly 80,000 US troops across Europe will be lower than the continent’s leaders have feared, according to people familiar with the matter.]]></description>\n            <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-14/pentagon-eyes-smaller-troop-cuts-across-europe-in-reversal</link>\n            <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">TOEK9XT9NJLS00</guid>\n            <dc:creator><![CDATA[Andrea Palasciano, Courtney McBride and Andra Timu]]></dc:creator>\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:59:09 GMT</pubDate>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <title><![CDATA[Fetterman Says Van Hollen as Senate Leader Would Be ‘Troubling’]]></title>\n            <description><![CDATA[Senator John Fetterman suggested he may reevaluate his role in the Democratic Party if Senator Chris Van Hollen were elected majority leader, citing his colleague’s criticism of Israel.]]></description>\n            <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-14/fetterman-says-van-hollen-as-senate-leader-would-be-troubling</link>\n            <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">TOI1NGT96OSH00</guid>\n            <dc:creator><![CDATA[Cam Kettles]]></dc:creator>\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:46:23 GMT</pubDate>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <title><![CDATA[Ukraine Hit Pumping Station, Russia Strikes Naftogaz Plant]]></title>\n            <description><![CDATA[Ukraine claimed a hit on a major crude-pipeline hub in the Samara region, deep within Russia, while Kremlin forces on Saturday targeted a Naftogaz Group facility in central Ukraine as regular air attacks continue on energy infrastructure.]]></description>\n            <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-14/ukraine-says-it-hit-oil-pumping-station-in-russia-s-samara</link>\n            <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">TOHM86KIP3ID00</guid>\n            <dc:creator><![CDATA[Bloomberg News]]></dc:creator>\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:56:16 GMT</pubDate>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <title><![CDATA[Hungary Finds $20 Million Cash in Probe of Orban Minister]]></title>\n            <description><![CDATA[Hungarian investigators found millions in cash stashed in forests, barns and warehouses around the country, piling pressure on an opposition dogged by swelling allegations of corruption by allies of former Premier Viktor Orban.]]></description>\n            <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-13/hungary-finds-20-million-cash-stash-in-probe-on-orban-minister</link>\n            <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">TOGIMPT96OSP00</guid>\n            <dc:creator><![CDATA[Thomas Escritt and Andras Gergely]]></dc:creator>\n            <pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:31:02 GMT</pubDate>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <title><![CDATA[Looking Beyond Tech’s Recent Market Turmoil]]></title>\n            <description><![CDATA[Ritholtz Wealth Management founder and CIO Barry Ritholtz tells Bloomberg This Weekend why recent volatility in technology stocks does not necessarily signal broader weakness in the US equity market. Speaking with hosts David Gura and Christina Ruffini, Ritholtz looks at the S&P 500’s resilience, historical market performance following midterm elections and the data investors should consider when assessing what could come next for stocks. (Source: Bloomberg)]]></description>\n            <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-11-14/looking-beyond-tech-s-recent-market-turmoil-video</link>\n            <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">TOHYQCKGZAIO00</guid>\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:54:12 GMT</pubDate>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <title><![CDATA[Miller’s White House Ascent Rattles Mexico Trade Negotiators]]></title>\n            <description><![CDATA[A new and not-so-friendly face is poised to loom over the negotiating table where the US and Mexico are still trying to hammer out a trade deal.]]></description>\n            <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-14/miller-s-white-house-ascent-rattles-mexico-trade-negotiators</link>\n            <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">TO9D2HKJH6V500</guid>\n            <dc:creator><![CDATA[Gonzalo Soto]]></dc:creator>\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:30:00 GMT</pubDate>\n        </item>\n    </channel>\n</rss>","fetchedAt":"2026-11-15T12:59:07.864Z"},"cbs":{"xml":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<rss version=\"2.0\"\n        \txmlns:content=\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\"\n\txmlns:wfw=\"http://wellformedweb.org/CommentAPI/\"\n\txmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\"\n\txmlns:atom=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom\"\n\txmlns:sy=\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/syndication/\"\n\txmlns:slash=\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/slash/\"\n    xmlns:s=\"https://www.cbsnews.com/\"\n\n    xmlns:media=\"http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/\"\n>\n    <channel>\n        \n        \n               \n\n            <title>Home - CBSNews.com</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/</link>\n    <description>Headlines From CBSNews.com</description>\n    <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:56:00 -0500</pubDate>\n    <ttl>5</ttl>\n            \n                    <item>\n                \n    <title>U.S. reportedly floated trading Ukrainian land for NATO membership</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/ukraine-russia-war-nato-us-donbas/</link>\n    <description>The Ukrainian president said he would put the question of a potential exchange to the people if certain guarantees were in place.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:33:32 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets2.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/15/f8840d9f-c1e1-4c1a-8e6c-9076d3fa8a45/thumbnail/60x60/310b6cc2036d83ab35dbd329d29aa6b8/gettyimages-2304304126.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">ef6307c2-17d5-4273-8b83-1219c55fc286</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>UPS plane, passenger jet collide on Miami airport taxiway</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/ups-plane-copa-airlines-jet-collide-miami-international-airport/</link>\n    <description>A UPS cargo plane and a Copa Airlines jet carrying 172 people collided while taxiing at Miami International Airport, leaving two passengers with minor injuries.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:24:57 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets1.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/15/a3de3c5e-4473-48af-873a-617ae7909089/thumbnail/60x60/089e78ec0cc08ec07986656a06348d5d/cbsmiami-copa-ups-main-12.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">e5e6085d-8ad9-47db-961a-ce2b49c6715f</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Flights expected to normalize by tonight after ground stop. Here&#039;s what to know</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/faa-ground-stop-canceled-flights-travelers-what-we-know/</link>\n    <description>Officials attributed the ground stop to aging system infrastructure and legacy technology.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:19:42 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets3.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/09/21/6e00213c-d3cb-4aa7-8d3d-6f9514f34261/thumbnail/60x60/99765ea3d51615b246c43b70cd487f03/gettyimages-2289770513.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">e3c38d29-19bd-4d3a-ae5a-f6fdbad7d366</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Bahrain says it intercepted Iranian strikes, Tehran targets U.S. assets</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/us-iran-war-trump-nuclear-material-no-deal/</link>\n    <description>The attacks come after the U.S. carried out minor strikes on Iran&#039;s Qeshm island in recent weeks.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:04:17 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets3.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/15/5f3361e9-d00f-47de-a6a2-571908cce626/thumbnail/60x60/6223b62671930e99eb88b027ebad1e9f/gettyimages-2304363306.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">05e71002-d660-4b5a-80f9-2063ad924e0d</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>&quot;48 Hours&quot; show schedule</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/48-hours/episode-schedule/</link>\n    <description>&quot;48 Hours&quot; uncovers the narrative behind true crime cases with unmatched reporting and suspense.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:05:04 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets2.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2022/09/22/23f1bcdf-10e4-46e5-914c-8b0bfca1a801/thumbnail/60x60/e514f8997999f497d5be8a9bce09b3f6/48hrs-thumbprint.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">a5fa8f0e-8c88-11e2-b06b-024c619f5c3d</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Oregon community suspects foul play when beloved shopkeeper disappears</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/susan-phoenix-lane-fournier-mount-hood-oregon-murder-48-hours/</link>\n    <description>When Susan &quot;Phoenix&quot; Lane and her two dogs went missing from Welches, Oregon, in the foothills of Mount Hood, her friends and family suspected foul play almost immediately.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:05:03 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets1.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/11/adf81817-996c-426d-bb91-1583b57c0a2e/thumbnail/60x60/459480f30f5f39e4516af92002124c69/lane-fornier-full.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">74653574-cec0-4e28-83d1-a2a0f70cdd05</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>How Trump administration responded to FAA ground stop</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/faa-ground-stop-trump-admin-response/</link>\n    <description>President Trump was informed within 30 minutes after the Federal Aviation Administration imposed a nationwide ground stop Friday afternoon, according to U.S. officials.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:16:17 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets1.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/15/2ae4d056-3f2b-4a69-97fc-d21f31da9442/thumbnail/60x60/ae0d964495069034666d67a6be5c35cf/gettyimages-2304597953.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">3c805c8e-7471-4c5d-8a75-1329e3358ac4</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Federal judge blocks Trump from closing historic D.C. golf course, for now</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/judge-blocks-east-potomac-park-dc-closing/</link>\n    <description>U.S. District Judge Ana Reyes ruled that the Trump administration cannot close East Potomac Park in Washington, D.C., for now.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:57:07 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets2.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/10/30/38651af2-b1d5-4fd2-8af5-5b8c16c539ee/thumbnail/60x60/cc932ca3ccae44fbf708aa11ff30da65/gettyimages-2301844335.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">a50d03a2-6bac-4299-a6ac-7eb02336be21</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>This week on &quot;Sunday Morning&quot; (Nov. 15)</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/this-week-on-sunday-morning-nov-15-2026/</link>\n    <description>A look at the features for this week&#039;s broadcast of the Emmy-winning program, hosted by Jane Pauley.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:35:38 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets1.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/13/43254545-bb19-448e-ad54-ad663bb629e1/thumbnail/60x60/21d0663b12b6ea9e784d4d6b569a88af/smith-odc-sun.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">205bf62d-62ba-48a8-b883-edaaf3659e12</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Murder at Mount Hood</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/video/111426-48-hours-murder-at-mount-hood/</link>\n    <description>When a beloved Oregon woman goes missing, her community in the mountains bands together to help solve the case. &quot;48 Hours&quot; correspondent Peter Van Sant reports.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:00:00 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets2.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/14/70a8968b-f68a-4059-9bf0-b41a33308047/thumbnail/60x60/383022e2e589f59bb5d35fb840536738/lane-fornier-full.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">3e90e903-4676-41d3-b6b6-331b03d49193</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Evacuation lifted after bomb threat near industrial plant in Illinois</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/peoria-illinois-bomb-threat-evacuation/</link>\n    <description>Police said the device had been rendered safe and residents were allowed to return to their homes.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:28:38 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets3.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/14/c7d3f410-adef-4541-93bd-a8dcd11176d3/thumbnail/60x60/b3243af659c38a39e806561c021a52bb/untitled-design-2026-11-14t065846-665.png</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">7b3cf910-a922-42c5-a735-3b81f2be728e</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Watch: Massive waves, flooding batter Northern California</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/video/videos-show-waves-flooding-batter-northern-california/</link>\n    <description>High surf and coastal flooding battered Northern California from Thursday through Saturday, sending massive waves crashing onto shorelines in San Francisco, Pacifica and Santa Cruz.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:23:22 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets1.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/15/883a71bc-7622-47f4-8bbf-d0a8ae039a85/thumbnail/60x60/56791035547cd704565aa48a9ece48cf/thumb-2.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">b56178a7-8dee-40b7-9dea-63b121e7fc97</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>3 killed when SUV crashes into North Hollywood food stand</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/north-hollywood-food-stand-crash-metro-bus-stop-lankershim-chandler-boulevard/</link>\n    <description>At least three people were killed and two others were severely injured when an SUV crashed into a food stand near a Metro bus stop in North Hollywood.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:53:25 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets2.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/11/f2ecf391-3557-4907-89dd-1c8a0e2c9fe3/thumbnail/60x60/63edd2d4ea3a0cfaf6e63782906b404e/gettyimages-2304532161.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">e5944175-7ca8-4413-b3aa-1d2675b8cad0</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>5th Canadian soldier dies weeks after fire on military base</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/5th-canadian-soldier-dies-wainwright-base-fire/</link>\n    <description>Pvt. William Douglas Dal Bianco died Friday at a hospital in Ontario, where he had been receiving treatment since the Oct. 17 fire at Canadian Forces Base Wainwright in Alberta, the military said.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:44:46 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets1.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/10/23/bf208e38-37ff-425a-95e4-ea451b9bbd5d/thumbnail/60x60/c1154136294081c7a5e2387b606c3dd6/gettyimages-2300376298.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">16af888a-de57-43f8-8e94-66efbab7772a</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>SpaceX pulls off first Starship recovery from orbit in spectacular fashion</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/spacex-catch-starship-rocket/</link>\n    <description>It was the first recovery of a Starship from orbit, a major milestone for a rocket SpaceX founder Elon Musk says will dramatically lower launch costs.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:06:59 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets1.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/14/61d3debe-ec5c-4680-8b32-df4e75a3453c/thumbnail/60x60/6c244762af8779fdde14df58908ef88c/121426-entry1.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">abf2f1db-6404-49d1-a9fb-f0cfcf8b8c4f</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Passengers rescued after tanker hit river cruise in New Orleans</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/tanker-cruise-collision-mississippi-river-new-orleans/</link>\n    <description>A tanker struck a river cruise ship on the Mississippi River near the Port of New Orleans Friday, partially submerging the passenger boat.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:05:04 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets2.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/13/ba59891d-9b26-4381-beee-7a4c061e552d/thumbnail/60x60/f3882275ce781379024dbc57d475d714/ap26317811767503.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">5790fcf0-dfbf-4684-846b-231c5b46dee1</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>U.S. facilitating direct engagement between Europe and Russia</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/us-europe-russia-engagement-ukraine-war/</link>\n    <description>President Trump&#039;s senior envoy and son-in-law, Jared Kushner, said they are also preparing for the next round of trilateral talks.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:07:08 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets1.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/14/6b7c9a1c-cf22-4bc0-a784-14264f608fb4/thumbnail/60x60/77edd88730a42402cbafc177504462df/ap26316810454758.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">1daa865d-9c7d-4240-b4ce-d29097a3d93a</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>&quot;Face the Nation with Margaret Brennan&quot; guests for Nov. 15, 2026</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/face-the-nation-guests-11-15-2026/</link>\n    <description>This week&#039;s guests include Secretary of Transportation Sean Duffy, Republican Sen. Bill Cassidy, Democratic Rep. Jim Himes and Republican Rep. John Moolenaar.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:35:00 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets1.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/04/22/b7af3bf5-80e0-4dac-93de-cd2a961e536b/thumbnail/60x60/a574b2bbf834d3dd3050571c8b5e5c37/cbsn-fusion-transportation-secretary-sean-duffy-makes-case-for-ai-safety-tools-reacts-to-spirit-concerns-thumbnail.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">58335ed9-4469-4118-8d7b-3f1692eb2c19</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Italy fines Meta $880 million over accessing users&#039; photos</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/italy-fines-meta-880-million-users-photos/</link>\n    <description>The country&#039;s data protection authority said Meta accessed users&#039; photos without their &quot;specific&quot; consent.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:33:08 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets2.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/08/27/14627318-b211-4ac4-b61d-2fbcf4111489/thumbnail/60x60/ad36721bf1bea1a90ebb3a2121791b81/gettyimages-2291623755.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">3b24b5dd-ae18-411b-abfa-806b3653bc9e</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Port of New Orleans sues tanker that hit riverboat cruise for $1 million</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/port-of-new-orleans-sues-tanker-riverboat-crash/</link>\n    <description>The port asked a judge to seize and sell the tanker that hit a riverboat cruise to cover the costs of repairs.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:56:43 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets2.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/13/ba59891d-9b26-4381-beee-7a4c061e552d/thumbnail/60x60/f3882275ce781379024dbc57d475d714/ap26317811767503.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">7fe0ea25-3ba6-495c-b31a-883b11e38d74</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>U.S. loses measles elimination status as cases surge nationwide</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/measles-elimination-status-united-states/</link>\n    <description>The United States has lost its official measles elimination status for the first time in 26 years. Here&#039;s what to know.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:42:15 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets1.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/07/a8f89dbf-6484-4ebf-863c-c4e91d42c3a6/thumbnail/60x60/f9862da3655275033e0feef152c0cddc/gettyimages-2259641072.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">4e1ba814-3fb5-4a65-b7f7-f7e706946495</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Investigators probe cause of deadly NYC building collapse</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/video/investigators-probe-cause-of-deadly-nyc-building-collapse/</link>\n    <description>New York City investigators are looking into whether anything criminal contributed to the deadly collapse of a building in Brooklyn.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:10:00 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets2.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/14/ef4fe3a3-0b3e-4cf9-b1fb-7504fccdad31/thumbnail/60x60/91f548541328bcd97c65ed060a856310/cbsn-fusion-investigators-probe-cause-of-deadly-nyc-building-collapse-thumbnail.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">308e8aab-7c32-4e13-9972-cfc99840efaf</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Air travel chaos after national ground stop lifted</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/video/air-travel-chaos-after-national-ground-stop-lifted/</link>\n    <description>Thousands of travelers are still dealing with flight delays and cancellations after the FAA lifted a national ground stop order. The ground stop highlighted a worsening air traffic network crisis, former NTSB chair Robert Sumwalt explains.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:31:00 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets1.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/14/e37afccb-c737-420d-b443-d35e5747a8f7/thumbnail/60x60/87d6afab3a2cdefc81d357ffac8c932a/cbsn-fusion-air-travel-chaos-after-national-ground-stop-lifted-thumbnail.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">001b13ab-31ec-4b6d-9c29-ab920aa03bcd</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Trump, Putin, Xi Jinping to meet in first trilateral of its kind</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-putin-xi-jinping-meeting-china-us-russia-talks/</link>\n    <description>President Trump is looking to talk about reducing nuclear arsenals in the first formal trilateral between the leaders of the U.S., China and Russia.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:59:00 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets2.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/14/ca3d845e-2e76-4093-9b96-5798868f6369/thumbnail/60x60/6c89897c53186ce8f9b60086f7717df6/gettyimages-2302566480.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">d315d58b-b749-43ce-83e9-317d455a69d3</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Microsoft says it &quot;restored service&quot; after major worldwide outage</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/microsoft-battling-major-outage/</link>\n    <description>A Microsoft outage involving services like Outlook and Teams impacted many users, companies and government services.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:32:05 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets3.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/13/3078adce-27fa-4f9b-b304-dbc4d6858df6/thumbnail/60x60/c1bfaf918f8eaccaafab8fd4a7c556c8/gettyimages-2302285784.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">8c622a8b-2fd7-4ddc-a5a2-23e5a4b395b5</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Trump says &quot;we don&#039;t need a deal with Iran&quot;</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-war-us-nuclear-strait-of-hormuz/</link>\n    <description>President Trump says the war with Iran has been won and &quot;we don&#039;t need a deal,&quot; as Tehran sticks to its demands and continues attacking ships.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:31:00 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets2.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/12/8b4712bb-7eec-4c3a-9551-bc1100bcb6e4/thumbnail/60x60/1e71fd2dbc26b0ef598d2a6bd1ef8259/oman-strait-hormuz-tanker-attack.png</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">bcf0bbe3-03df-4968-8daa-08d54303435b</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Van Hollen will challenge Schumer for Senate majority leader</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/chris-van-hollen-challenge-chuck-schumer-senate-majority-leader-democrat/</link>\n    <description>Democratic Sen. Chris Van Hollen of Maryland announced Thursday that he will challenge Sen. Chuck Schumer for Senate majority leader.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:58:38 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets3.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/10/8023000d-59ef-46a9-ba34-08164c04fcb8/thumbnail/60x60/e1691d2dbd5b24c56dfc861ca592f398/ap26176520488521.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">37a833b3-c742-4c53-91ad-57fa3c62c156</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Hegseth awards medal to soldier who reprimanded group near tomb</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/hegseth-medal-reprimand-tomb-of-the-unknown-soldier/</link>\n    <description>Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth awarded a medal to the service member who reprimanded his group for making noise at the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier​.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:04:50 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets1.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/12/3e03a3ba-436d-4aee-981b-0a5bbc12fe2e/thumbnail/60x60/adb317816925b65e8f48b93e0bcf03bc/screenshot-2026-11-12-at-11-43-20-am.png</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">cf3e839a-f05a-407b-bf54-e608e678e932</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Veterans in watercolor</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/video/veterans-in-watercolor/</link>\n    <description>For her project titled &quot;We the People,&quot; artist Mary Whyte set out to paint 50 veterans from 50 states. The men and women included in the exhibition, now at the City Gallery in Charleston, S.C., are as diverse as the nation they served. Martha Teichner reports.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sun, 10 Nov 2019 10:05:00 -0500</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets3.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/11/14/469834bc-609a-4b6b-9761-7688ef5ead63/thumbnail/60x60/25c1494abe6e104e790977fe20542fcb/veterans-in-watercolor-2019.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">cbf1d9d5-a984-45bc-98f3-482fbaf278e4</guid>\n        </item>\n            <item>\n                \n    <title>Preserving on canvas a vanishing way of life</title>\n    <link>https://www.cbsnews.com/news/preserving-on-canvas-a-vanishing-way-of-life/</link>\n    <description>Mary Whyte&#039;s paintings document the traditions, work and aura of the Southern U.S.</description>\n\n            <pubDate>Sun, 05 Sep 2010 09:17:00 -0400</pubDate>\n    \n                    \n\n\t    \t        <image>https://assets3.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2010/09/05/9deea106-a644-11e2-a3f0-029118418759/thumbnail/60x60/f4dad5f9c4b24801bbcac3a954317ef7/image6837345x.jpg</image>\n\t        \n    \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">a55d496a-8c88-11e2-b06b-024c619f5c3d</guid>\n        </item>\n        </channel>\n</rss>","fetchedAt":"2026-11-15T12:59:07.864Z"},"cnn":{"xml":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n    <rss version=\"2.0\"><channel>\n      <title>CNN Recent Headlines</title>\n      <link>https://www.cnn.com/</link>\n      <description>Recent CNN headlines with publisher timestamps</description>\n      \n      <item>\n        <title>US floated idea of Ukraine swapping land for NATO membership, Zelensky says</title>\n        <link>https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/14/europe/us-ukraine-zelensky-nato-intl</link>\n        <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:24:13 GMT</pubDate>\n        <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/14/europe/us-ukraine-zelensky-nato-intl</guid>\n      </item>\n    \n\n      <item>\n        <title>The systems used to keep America flying are ancient. That makes fixing the problem that much more difficult</title>\n        <link>https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/15/business/faa-tech-systems-us-government</link>\n        <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:00:15 GMT</pubDate>\n        <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/15/business/faa-tech-systems-us-government</guid>\n      </item>\n    \n\n      <item>\n        <title>A gunman took four lives at an Oregon elementary school. The families came back to reclaim it</title>\n        <link>https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/15/us/bend-oregon-silver-rail-elementary-return</link>\n        <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:30:15 GMT</pubDate>\n        <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/15/us/bend-oregon-silver-rail-elementary-return</guid>\n      </item>\n    \n\n      <item>\n        <title>Lindsay Clancy due in court for a hearing that should determine what her retrial may look like</title>\n        <link>https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/15/us/lindsay-clancy-retrial-court-hearing</link>\n        <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:00:15 GMT</pubDate>\n        <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/15/us/lindsay-clancy-retrial-court-hearing</guid>\n      </item>\n    \n    </channel></rss>","fetchedAt":"2026-11-15T12:59:07.864Z"},"fox":{"xml":"<rss xmlns:media=\"http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/\" xmlns:content=\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xmlns:atom=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom\" version=\"2.0\"> <channel> <title>Latest &amp; Breaking News on Fox News</title> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/</link> <description>Discover the latest breaking news feed with Fox. Find out what the latest news is and read about the latest news happening today.</description> <copyright>Copyright 2026 FOX News Network</copyright> <language>en-us</language> <pubDate> Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:49:20 -0500 </pubDate>  <image> <url>https://global.fncstatic.com/static/orion/styles/img/fox-news/logos/fox-news-desktop.png</url> <title>Latest &amp; Breaking News on Fox News</title> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/</link> </image>  <atom:link rel=\"self\" href=\"https://moxie.foxnews.com/google-publisher/latest.xml\" type=\"application/rss+xml\"/> <atom:link rel=\"hub\" href=\"https://pubsubhubbub.appspot.com/\" xmlns:atom=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom\"/>     <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-betting/bets-breakfast-looking-winners-nfl-early-game-munich</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-betting/bets-breakfast-looking-winners-nfl-early-game-munich</guid> <title>Bets and Breakfast: Looking for winners in the NFL’s early game in Munich</title>  <description>Patriots vs. Lions Munich betting preview: Why the Patriots moneyline at +130 is the play, plus three player props to pair with it.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;Set the alarm and put the coffee on. The NFL is back in Germany Sunday morning, with the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/sports/nfl/new-england-patriots&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;New England Patriots&lt;/a&gt; and Detroit Lions kicking off at 9:30 a.m. ET from Allianz Arena in Munich.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On the surface, this looks like an easy read. Detroit is 6-2 and riding a four-game winning streak. New England is 5-4 and coming off a 45-27 beating at home by Green Bay, a game where &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/person/drake-maye&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Drake Maye&lt;/a&gt; threw three interceptions, got sacked four times and watched the Packers turn four takeaways into three touchdowns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The betting market has seen all of that, and it has made its call. I think that call creates value on the other side.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/drake-maye-tells-reporters-dont-know-what-theyre-talking-about-germany-press-conference&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DRAKE MAYE TELLS REPORTERS THEY DON&apos;T KNOW &apos;WHAT THEY&apos;RE TALKING ABOUT&apos; DURING GERMANY PRESS CONFERENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Patriots +130 | Lions -150&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Spread: &lt;/strong&gt;Lions -2.5&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Total: &lt;/strong&gt;49.5 to 51.5 depending on the book&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best bet: &lt;/strong&gt;Patriots moneyline (+130)&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Props:&lt;/strong&gt; Hunter Henry over 35.5 receiving yards (-115), Drake Maye over 25.5 rushing yards (-115), Mack Hollins over 34.5 receiving yards (-115)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sunday, Nov. 15, 9:30 a.m. ET, Allianz Arena, Munich, [TV]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/human-vs-chatgpt-nfl-week-10-betting-picks-ice-cold-human-seeks-rebound-ai-gains-ground&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HUMAN VS. CHATGPT NFL WEEK 10 BETTING PICKS: ICE-COLD HUMAN SEEKS A REBOUND AS AI GAINS GROUND&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The moneyline split is about as lopsided as it gets. At one major sportsbook, 95.85% of the moneyline money is &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/sports/nfl/detroit-lions&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;on Detroit&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;That’s a market reacting to the last game it watched. Everyone saw Green Bay put up 478 yards on New England, and everyone saw Detroit win four straight. Nobody wants to lay money on a team that just got embarrassed at home.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The spread tells a more interesting story. Detroit has drawn 68% of the spread tickets, but 55% of the actual money has come in on New England. When the bigger bets go one way and the ticket count goes the other, that’s usually a sign of where the sharper money is. The line has moved to match, dropping from Detroit -3 to -2.5 during the week.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The casual crowd is all over the Lions. The bigger money is quietly backing the Patriots.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is the number that anchors the bet. New England is 6-0 in the game after a loss since the start of last season. Every time this team has been knocked down, it has come back and won the next week.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-betting/underdog-promo-code-foxnews-play-10-get-50-ahead-49ers-raiders-patriots-packers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;The Green Bay loss&lt;/a&gt; looks worse on paper than it was. The Patriots turned it over four times, and those giveaways turned straight into points. New England averages 2.11 giveaways per game this season, which is the real problem. But the Patriots are 3-0 when Maye doesn’t throw an interception, and 10-1 since 2025 when they allow fewer than three sacks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Turnovers can swing wildly from week to week, and a team’s ability to bounce back is a much more reliable trait. That’s what you’re betting here.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Lions’ four-game run is real, but the offense driving it has cooled off. Detroit scored 20, 19 and 19 points in its last three games, and its last three games all went under the total. That’s a long way from the offense that opened the season going over in each of its first five.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Lions’ defense has carried the streak, allowing 21, 17, 15 and 9 points in the last four games. It’s also a defense that allows 24.2 points per game away from Ford Field. Munich is technically a Detroit home game, but nobody will mistake Allianz Arena for Ford Field.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLICK HERE FOR MORE OUTKICK SPORTS COVERAGE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There’s also a history worth knowing. Favorites are 5-2 straight up in &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/nfl-owners-approve-record-10-international-games-2027-sights-expansion-abroad&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;international games&lt;/a&gt;, but only 3-4 against the spread, and five of seven have finished under the closing total. Overseas games tend to be tighter than the market expects, which favors the team getting points and a plus price.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If the Patriots bounce back, these three props should come along with them.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hunter Henry over 35.5 receiving yards (-115). &lt;/strong&gt;This is the best matchup on the board for New England. Detroit allows 25.1 fantasy points per game to tight ends, the most in the NFL. The league average is 13.7. Henry has gone over his longest-reception number in 14 of his last 20 games, and he’s Maye’s safety valve when the pocket gets crowded.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://link.podtrac.com/ccs_article&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE CRAIG CARTON SHOW–UNFILTERED, UNAPOLOGETIC AND UNMISSABLE. DOWNLOAD HIS DAILY PODCAST NOW!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drake Maye over 25.5 rushing yards (-115).&lt;/strong&gt; Detroit averages 3.38 sacks per game, and New England’s offensive line allows pressure on 36.4% of snaps. That’s a recipe for Maye escaping the pocket. If the Patriots want to avoid turnovers, the cleanest answer is letting their quarterback pick up yards with his legs rather than forcing throws into coverage.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mack Hollins over 34.5 receiving yards (-115).&lt;/strong&gt; Hollins has gone over his receiving yards number in 10 of his last 12 games. With A.J. Brown most likely a bit limited, Hollins has been the steady target Maye can count on.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Detroit is the better team on paper this week. But the market is paying more for the Lions’ recent record than for how they’ve actually been playing, and it’s discounting a Patriots team that has answered every loss for two seasons.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;At +130, with heavy money on the other side and a team that doesn’t lose two in a row, I’ll take my breakfast with a side of New England.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Give me the &lt;strong&gt;Patriots moneyline &lt;/strong&gt;(+130).&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/10/931/523/drake-maye-patriots-bears-soldier-field.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">aa2b1f6f-006c-5a38-9cac-34ea6488cd9f</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/nfl</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/nfl/new-england-patriots</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/nfl/detroit-lions</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/betting</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/outkick-sports</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/outkick-betting</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:49:20 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/us/faa-says-air-travel-should-be-back-normal-sunday-after-nationwide-ground-stop</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/us/faa-says-air-travel-should-be-back-normal-sunday-after-nationwide-ground-stop</guid> <title>FAA says air travel should be back to normal Sunday after nationwide ground stop</title>  <description>FAA Administrator Bryan Bedford says the worst is over after the longest nationwide ground stop in 25 years disrupted around 15,000 flights.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;The U.S. air travel schedule should return to normal by the end of Sunday, according to the Federal Aviation Administration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;FAA Administrator Bryan Bedford declared Saturday that &quot;the worst is behind us&quot; after the U.S. saw its longest nationwide ground stop in 25 years this weekend.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Transportation Sec. Sean Duffy says the situation arose when contractor L3Harris Technologies Inc. was replacing old copper wiring in the air traffic control system with new fiber wiring, causing a system overload.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/politics/faa-unveils-new-air-traffic-controller-hiring-plan-chief-warned-system-chronically-understaffed&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FAA UNVEILS NEW AIR TRAFFIC CONTROLLER HIRING PLAN AFTER CHIEF WARNED SYSTEM WAS ‘CHRONICALLY UNDERSTAFFED’&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The work led to &quot;intermittent&quot; communications and radar gaps, prompting the government to shut down air traffic for more than four hours. Officials were investigating whether contractor &quot;incompetence&quot; or a faulty router was the cause,&quot; he said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Our contractor didn’t meet the moment or the equipment didn’t meet the moment,&quot; Duffy said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/politics/exclusive-trumps-faa-touts-new-ai-powered-tool-helping-thousands-passengers-avoid-flight-delays&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EXCLUSIVE: TRUMP&apos;S FAA TOUTS NEW AI-POWERED TOOL HELPING THOUSANDS OF PASSENGERS AVOID FLIGHT DELAYS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The nationwide stop was &lt;a href=&quot;https://apnews.com/article/science-federal-aviation-administration-business-9e277db75130cc7e4d4b6c6a7bdaad7c&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;the first since January 2023&lt;/a&gt; , when a &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/media/former-top-faa-official-warns-48-hour-recovery-aging-tech-overwhelmed-ground-stop&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;key FAA computer system&lt;/a&gt; that sends notices to pilots malfunctioned, and the second since the Sept. 11, 2001, terror attacks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The FAA issued the &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/travel/4-critical-travel-issues-those-still-scrambling-after-faa-nationwide-ground-stop&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;ground stop order&lt;/a&gt; on Friday afternoon.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/updated-start-times-college-football-games-affected-faa-ground-stop-broken-down-conference&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UPDATED START TIMES FOR COLLEGE FOOTBALL GAMES AFFECTED BY FAA GROUND STOP, BROKEN DOWN BY CONFERENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The ground stop was lifted at 8:15 p.m. ET Friday, but the ripple effect felt by airline crews and passengers lasted with residual delays continuing to affect airport operations, ultimately impacting some 15,000 flights Friday and Saturday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;You will continue to see some delays and cancellations as carriers reschedule flights and reposition aircraft/crews where they are needed most,&quot; Secretary of Transportation Sean Duffy said in a post on X this weekend.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/travel/were-going-die-passengers-recount-midair-terror-before-emergency-landing&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&apos;WE&apos;RE GOING TO DIE&apos;: PASSENGERS RECOUNT MIDAIR TERROR BEFORE EMERGENCY LANDING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Travelers should continue to check their &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/travel/legal-expert-details-travelers-entitled-massive-east-coast-flight-cancellations&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;flight status&lt;/a&gt; directly with their airlines for real-time updates, he noted.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Check those, be in touch with your airline, check their websites, look at online monitoring tools,&quot; Gary Leff, a Texas-based travel industry expert and author of the blog &quot;View From the Wing,&quot; told Fox News Digital.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;Fox News&apos; Sadie Chafe and The Associated Press contributed to this report.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/faa-ground-stop.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">d468e948-2bd4-5ad0-bf39-ed5f2b5bd9b4</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/world/disasters/transportation</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/travel/general/airports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/science/air-and-space</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/news-events</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/us</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:36:46 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/politics/inside-senate-gops-tense-post-election-reckoning-thune-clashes-republican-critics</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/politics/inside-senate-gops-tense-post-election-reckoning-thune-clashes-republican-critics</guid> <title>Inside Senate GOP&apos;s tense post-election reckoning as Thune clashes with Republican critics</title>  <description>Senate Republicans kept John Thune as leader by acclamation after a heated closed-door meeting that some lawmakers compared to &amp;quot;Festivus.&amp;quot;</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;Senate Republicans huddled for hours on end to define their remaining time in power and determine if the leadership they had backed so far was the right choice moving forward into a new era in Washington, D.C.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Some closed-door meetings over the last nearly two years Republicans have controlled the Senate have been animated, with policy pitches devolving into shouting matches — President &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/person/donald-trump&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Donald Trump&lt;/a&gt; and Sen. Bill Cassidy, R-La., infamously sparred over the Iran war earlier this year.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This confab, their first since Senate Minority Leader &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/person/chuck-schumer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Chuck Schumer,&lt;/a&gt; D-N.Y., and Democrats roared back into the majority, was different. In part, it was meant to develop a plan that would carry them through the final weeks of this year — that was agreed upon during the meeting, but not without its own drama after the fact on who could lay claim to the GOP’s 54-day blitz.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/politics/senate-gop-rebellion-fizzles-thune-keeps-power-despite-historic-midterm-massacre&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SENATE GOP REBELLION FIZZLES AS THUNE KEEPS POWER DESPITE HISTORIC MIDTERM MASSACRE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It was also a test to see if Republicans wanted to keep Senate Majority Leader &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/person/john-thune&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;John Thune,&lt;/a&gt; R-S.D., as their leader, or delay until a challenger appeared.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;But Republicans pushing for a delay acknowledged part of the problem: Who would want the job?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;I got the job because nobody else wants it,&quot; Thune told Fox News Digital after the dust settled in the Old Senate Chamber.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;And he did, along with much of the same leadership team that Senate Republicans elected when they won the majority two years ago, by acclamation, meaning no lawmaker objected to their leadership slate.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Some told Fox News Digital it was like &quot;Festivus,&quot; the holiday etched into Gen-Xers&apos; brains from &quot;Seinfeld&quot; known for its airing of grievances. Others described it as a frank, needed debrief as the GOP picks through the debris of &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/opinion/mark-halperin-republicans-bracing-wipeout-heres-who-theyll-blame-happens&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Election Night.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/politics/gop-senator-withholds-support-thune-leadership-showdown-looms&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GOP SENATOR WITHHOLDS SUPPORT FOR THUNE AS LEADERSHIP SHOWDOWN LOOMS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;It really was, to be honest with you, as profound as the loss was last week. I would have expected more emotions, which I consider to be a good sign,&quot; Sen. Thom Tillis, R-N.C., told Fox News Digital. &quot;But I think it&apos;s almost — It&apos;s self-governing because nobody can dispute that it&apos;s a problem.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Now it&apos;s not like you&apos;re looking for the silver lining,&quot; he continued. &quot;It doesn&apos;t exist. It is what it is, and you&apos;ve got to react.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;But there were some &quot;testy&quot; moments, particularly between Thune and Sen. Ron Johnson, R-Wis., the driving force behind the push to &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/politics/senate-gop-rebels-move-delay-leadership-vote-demand-reckoning-after-midterm-disaster&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;delay leadership elections.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For Thune, the main question was what anyone else in the Senate GOP would have done differently in his shoes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;I just think that you come through an election like this and everybody&apos;s looking for scapegoats and there&apos;s a lot of blame casting that goes on, and I just wanted to get up and basically defend what we had done and accomplished,&quot; Thune said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;And I think the operative question is, tell me what you would do differently? Both on the political side and the legislative side. So we had a good, we had a robust conversation, and it does. It always gets a little bit testy in the back and forth, but I thought that, by and large, the discussion was very candid, and certainly gave everybody an opportunity to be heard.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/politics/congress-returns-brutal-lame-duck-stretch-shutdown-deadline-leadership-races-closet-full-s&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CONGRESS RETURNS TO BRUTAL LAME-DUCK STRETCH WITH SHUTDOWN DEADLINE, LEADERSHIP RACES: &apos;CLOSET IS FULL OF S—&apos;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Johnson acknowledged that he was &quot;prone to interrupting, I’m rude that way,&quot; and told Fox News Digital that he was sure Thune was &quot;not happy that I did that,&quot; but assured that there was no &quot;animus&quot; between the two.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;In politics, everything has to be so black and white, and, unfortunately, for our base, the way to really rev them up is inter-conference fighting, which is not helpful,&quot; Johnson said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;So, again, I didn&apos;t really like doing this, but it had to be done,&quot; he continued. &quot;I mean, we had to, and in the end, I think, resulted in a very, very good conversation and pretty well revealed we&apos;re just lucky to have anybody who wants those jobs.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sen. Steve Daines, R-Mont., told Fox News Digital that Thune showed &quot;moments of exceptional leadership&quot; in the heat of the meeting.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;He noted that the top Republican&apos;s rebuttal reminded lawmakers of the &quot;ebb and flow of the politics in our country,&quot; dating back to 1986, when former President Ronald Reagan, then entering his &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/opinion/trey-gowdy-midterms-painful-lesson-republicans-cant-skip-learning&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;final midterm election&lt;/a&gt; similar to Trump, lost eight seats in the upper chamber.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Obama lost nine Senate seats in 2014, it looks like we&apos;re going to lose eight, depending on &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/politics/nine-key-races-could-decide-who-controls-senate-where-stand&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;what happens in Alaska,&quot;&lt;/a&gt; Daines said. &quot;So it&apos;s within the kind of the historic norms of going back and forth.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;And the leader forcefully laid that out and then talked about what he needed to do going forward to unify and eventually reclaim the majority,&quot; he continued.&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/thune-senate-republican-leadership-elections.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">87bf7d1a-4232-5ca3-b136-e6dfae185ac8</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/politics</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/politics/senate</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/person/john-thune</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/politics/elections/republicans</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us/congress</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/politics</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:00:37 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/entertainment/sammy-kershaw-accepts-cma-apology-country-stars-speak-red-carpet-access</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/entertainment/sammy-kershaw-accepts-cma-apology-country-stars-speak-red-carpet-access</guid> <title>Sammy Kershaw accepts CMA apology after country stars speak out over red carpet access</title>  <description>Sammy Kershaw&amp;apos;s CMA Awards red carpet denial ignited a firestorm among country music artists who say the industry sidelines legends for influencers.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;Sammy Kershaw and Rodney Atkins spoke out about being denied permission to walk the red carpet at this year’s &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/entertainment/events/cma-awards&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Country Music Association Awards&lt;/a&gt;, prompting criticism over how the organization treats veteran country artists.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Last week, Kershaw, 68, shared a statement on Instagram in which he revealed that the organization rejected his request to walk the carpet at the upcoming ceremony with his wife, Mendy, a decision that he called &quot;extremely hurtful, embarrassing and very disappointing.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Following Kershaw&apos;s post, Atkins, 57, announced that he and his wife, Rose Falcon, were also denied red carpet access and would no longer be attending the ceremony, which will be held on Nov. 18 and marks the CMAs&apos; milestone 60th anniversary.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/entertainment/country-star-cody-johnson-says-nashville-wanted-change-him-before-success&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COUNTRY STAR CODY JOHNSON SAYS NASHVILLE WANTED TO CHANGE HIM BEFORE SUCCESS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;After facing backlash from other country musicians and fans, the CMA issued a response in which the organization explained that its red carpet criteria helps manage limited space and security needs and apologized to those who &quot;felt excluded by those decisions.&quot; The CMA also added that it was speaking with Kershaw&apos;s team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On Tuesday, Kershaw shared a post in which he said that he had accepted an apology from the CMA as well as an invitation for himself and Mendy to walk the red carpet and attend the ceremony.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The controversy sparked an uproar among country artists, who argued that the CMA has welcomed influencers, actors and crossover celebrities onto the red carpet while sidelining veteran performers. In addition, other country musicians raised broader concerns about how the industry as a whole recognizes artists who helped shape the genre.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In his initial post on Nov. 5, Kershaw &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/p/DfYXtulxXXO/?hl=en&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;wrote&lt;/a&gt; that the denial of his request to walk the CMAs carpet &quot;really hurts me.&quot; He explained that he learned of the rejection just two weeks ahead of the awards show after he and Mendy had already rearranged his touring schedule and booked flights and hotels.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/entertainment&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LIKE WHAT YOU&apos;RE READING? CLICK HERE FOR MORE ENTERTAINMENT NEWS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;My wife, Mendy, and I don&apos;t get to attend these events very often, due to touring and schedule conflicts,&quot; Kershaw wrote at the time. &quot;She was really looking forward to us sharing a special evening together celebrating &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/entertainment/genres/country&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;country music&lt;/a&gt;. Then, to find out I was denied the red carpet two weeks before the show, after being strung along for several months and expecting we would be attending, WTF?&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kershaw pointed to his decades-long career and longstanding relationship with the CMA to question why he was excluded. He cited his more than 50 years in the music business, millions of records sold, over two dozen Billboard hits, a past CMA Horizon Award nomination and his status as a &quot;lifetime CMA member&quot; since 1992.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The musician also noted that he previously &quot;donated&quot; his time to perform at &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/entertainment/events/cma-fest&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;CMA Fest&lt;/a&gt;, and that he hoped he had earned the right to walk the carpet alongside his wife just as they had in the past.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;I’m blessed to still be out on tour every year, performing for the greatest fans in the world doing what I love,&quot; Kershaw wrote. &quot;I believe there should be room to recognize the artists who have spent their lives contributing to this organization’s success.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;I love country music, but never in a million years would I think that a successful country music entertainer (and I’m not the only one) would not be able to walk the red carpet. It’s extremely hurtful, embarrassing and very disappointing. I guess the next time I attend the CMA’s, it will be in tribute after I’m gone, if I’m lucky,&quot; he concluded.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Two days after Kershaw&apos;s post, Atkins shared a video in which he revealed that he and his wife, who is also a longtime CMA member, had also been excluded from the CMAs red carpet and decided to skip the event.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Well, I found out that Sammy Kershaw and I have something in common this year. Neither one of us got approved to walk the CMA awards red carpet,&quot; he began.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;When I heard about Sammy, I thought, &apos;What a shame. He&apos;s a great guy, sweetheart of a dude. Spent his life representing country music.&apos; Then I found out the same thing happened to me,&quot; Atkins continued. &quot;And in a way, I get it. I&apos;ve always been kind of an outsider, maybe a shrub in the landscape of country music.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/entertainment/natalie-maines-anti-trump-tirade-zach-bryans-fence-climbing-clash-fuel-country-musics-biggest-feuds&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NATALIE MAINES’ ANTI-TRUMP TIRADE, ZACH BRYAN’S FENCE-CLIMBING CLASH FUEL COUNTRY MUSIC’S BIGGEST FEUDS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Atkins went on to emphasize that he was having his strongest touring year, that his album &quot;True South&quot; reached the second round of CMA voting for album of the year and that his latest single could extend his chart presence into a third decade.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In a statement &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/entertainment/rodney-atkins-warns-younger-generation-against-chasing-trends-losing-sight-what-matters&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;the musician&lt;/a&gt; shared alongside the video, Atkins expressed his gratitude to his fans &quot;who made this career possible.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;You&apos;ve always made me feel welcome in country music, and that&apos;s what matters most,&quot; he wrote.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;After more than 20 years as a CMA member and countless CMA Fests I’ve played for free, Rose and I were denied red carpet clearance, just like Sammy Kershaw. So we’ve decided not to attend this year’s CMA Awards,&quot; Atkins shared. &quot;I also believe the artists who helped build the foundation of country music, like Sammy Kershaw, deserve a place in its celebrations.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &quot;&quot;She Don’t Know She’s Beautiful&quot; singer‘s post was met with supportive comments from other country stars, including some from the younger generation that paid tribute to Kershaw for his foundational contributions to the industry.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;If you haven’t earned the right to be there then nobody has… disappointing to say the least,&quot; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/entertainment/country-star-riley-green-nearly-dove-crowd-after-fan-split-his-ear-open-during-performance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Riley Green&lt;/a&gt; wrote.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Carly Pearce commented, &quot;Many of us wouldn’t be here without artists like you…&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Jake Owen declared himself &quot;Team Sammy,&quot; while Granger Smith added, &quot;So sad for country music. I grieve for the old CMA.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;This is wild! I’ll give you my spot!!,&quot; Drew Bainbridge offered. &quot;You paved the way for all of us on that carpet.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Other artists questioned why influencers were invited to walk the carpet while Kershaw was denied.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Ugh this makes me sad for country music. Can we please bring back the legends and not influencers?&quot; Kylie Morgan wrote.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;They’ll let zero talent influencers walk the red carpet but not Sammy Kershaw? I hate it here,&quot; Meghan Patrick commented.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Veteran country star &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/entertainment/country-singer-mark-chesnutt-says-alcoholism-almost-killed-him-admits-he-drank-handle-vodka-day&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Mark Chesnutt&lt;/a&gt; reacted to Kershaw&apos;s snub by the CMA in a lengthy statement on Facebook in which he criticized the organization, arguing that it prioritizes celebrities from outside the genre over longtime country artists.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;So Sammy Kershaw won’t be allowed to walk the red carpet at the big CMA Awards,&quot; he wrote. &quot;Well that’s about right. The CMA doesn’t care about us old 90s guys any more.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;It’s a shame they don’t respect the stars that dominated the charts in the past thirty years or before that but they sure roll out the welcome mat for pop stars and Hollywood movie stars and even hip hop artists,&quot; he continued. &quot;Anything but country music gets the performance spots on the show.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Chesnutt also contrasted the country music industry&apos;s treatment of the genre’s history with the recognition received by rock icons.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Rock n Roll honors its history and respects its legends while country music industry executives seem to ignore its rich history and its legends,&quot; he wrote. &quot;Thank God there’s still a lot of people that love traditional country music. They keep coming to our shows and showing their love and respect for the music we’ve made for nearly forty years now and we’ll keep working for them and not for those who don’t matter to US!&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Country singer Pam Tillis, who also rose to fame in the 1990s, also addressed Kershaw&apos;s red carpet denial, though she clarified that her criticism was not solely directed at the CMA.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;So let’s talk about today’s drama in country music: Sammy Kershaw and the CMAs. I’m not going to single out the CMA, because this happens all the time in our business,&quot; she wrote in a post on Instagram. &quot;It’s the nature of our industry that the rising stars get the spotlight, just as we did at one point.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Tillis emphasized the importance of preserving a legacy, pointing to her own experience growing up as the daughter of country icon Mel Tillis.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;I learned early that a legacy doesn’t keep itself,&quot; she wrote. &quot;Somebody has to stand up and say, ‘This artist mattered. They made a contribution.’ I’ve done that for Daddy most of my life.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;She acknowledged that rising stars naturally receive attention, but argued that established performers still connect with generations of fans.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/entertainment/entertainment-quizzes&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PUT YOUR ENTERTAINMENT KNOWLEDGE TO THE TEST AND SEE HOW YOU SCORE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;And I’ll tell you what I’ve seen: the country audience is a multigenerational audience, and ‘90s country is still very viable, even if it isn’t always visible,&quot; she wrote. &quot;A lot of us have three generations of fans showing up to our shows, singing, whooping and hollering for our songs. Many of today’s artists are making it big with their own spin on the ‘90s sound.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;I dare say many of us have felt the sting of being passed over for this, that and the other, in order to create an image that’s only part of the picture,&quot; Tillis continued. &quot;I know &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/topic/up-and-country&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;today’s new artists&lt;/a&gt; need all the support they can get in such a crazy, competitive market. But legacy artists who want to show up can be the bridge between where this music came from and where it’s going.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Many of us never say anything about these slights,&quot; she added. &quot;We just keep on doing our thing. As an artist who is a lifetime CMA member, Sammy just spoke out.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On Monday, the CMA released a statement responding to the backlash and citing space and security criteria for red carpet management.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;In recent days, several artists and their fans have spoken out about this year’s CMA Awards red carpet guidelines,&quot; the organization wrote. &quot;Like any major televised event, the red carpet has criteria that exists to help manage limited space and the security needs for both the artists and the media. We are deeply sorry anyone felt excluded by those decisions.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Our organization’s mission is to honor the history and celebrate the excellence of Country Music,&quot; it continued. &quot;With this 60th anniversary year, we are working extra hard to simultaneously spotlight the last six decades, while also celebrating what has been a tremendous year in 2026. It’s not easy to do all of that in just one night, but we are up for the challenge.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;We also know this is about more than a red carpet, and we are committed to keep listening and keep finding ways to make sure all artists feel welcome and at home here,&quot; the CMA added. &quot;To that point, we are in touch with Sammy Kershaw’s team and look forward to continuing that conversation.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On Tuesday, Kershaw shared a positive update, revealing that CMA leadership had &quot;extended a sincere, heartfelt apology&quot; which he had accepted following a &quot;sincere and meaningful private conversation.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;The CMA has also extended an invitation for my wife, Mendy, and me to walk the red carpet and attend this year&apos;s awards alongside our fellow artists,&quot; he wrote. &quot;I am grateful for that invitation and appreciate their willingness to listen, acknowledge our concerns, and work toward a positive outcome.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/newsletters?cmpid=fnfirstnl&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GET ENTERTAINMENT SCOOP DELIVERED RIGHT TO YOUR EMAIL BY CLICKING HERE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kershaw also thanked fans, fellow artists and the country music community for their support. He explained that he originally spoke publicly because he was hurt, rather than seeking attention or controversy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &quot;Cadillac Style&quot; singer emphasized that the controversy was about more than his personal invitation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;This was never about the red carpet,&quot; he wrote. &quot;It was about recognizing and respecting those who dedicated their lives to this music and preserving the history and legacy that makes country music so special.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kershaw expressed his hopes that the conversations would produce lasting change in how legacy artists are recognized.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;You cannot celebrate 60 years of country music without celebrating the artists who helped build those 60 years,&quot; he wrote.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Country music has always been about honoring where we’ve come from while embracing where we’re going,&quot; Kershaw continued. &quot;I have nothing but respect for the incredible talent carrying country music into the future. Every generation of artists deserves its moment to shine, and I believe there’s room to celebrate all of them.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/sammy-kershaw.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">e5967356-c14e-5e4f-af71-52aec0754921</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/entertainment/genres/country</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/entertainment</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/entertainment/music</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/entertainment/events/cma-awards</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/entertainment</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:00:33 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/us/purge-masked-suspect-accused-killing-college-student-halloween-bash-sister-helps-nab-him</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/us/purge-masked-suspect-accused-killing-college-student-halloween-bash-sister-helps-nab-him</guid> <title>&apos;Purge&apos;-masked suspect accused of killing college student at Halloween bash — before his sister helps nab him</title>  <description>Omar Perez&amp;apos;s sister identified him using police photos and the family&amp;apos;s Life360 app after the University of Colorado Boulder student&amp;apos;s killing.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;Colorado police have identified the people sought in security footage released after a Halloween party shooting that killed a University of Colorado Boulder student, as prosecutors consider additional charges.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On Thursday, Boulder Police Public Information Officer Dionne Waugh confirmed to Fox News Digital that &quot;everyone in the photos and video we released&quot; has now been identified.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The primary suspect, Omar Perez, 18, &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/us/crime/homicide&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;faces murder and related charges&lt;/a&gt; in the death of Luca Hanlon, 19, following a deadly confrontation at an off-campus Oct. 31 party in Boulder’s University Hill neighborhood.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/us/mass-shooting-georgia-block-party-leaves-2-dead-35-injured&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MASS SHOOTING AT GEORGIA BLOCK PARTY LEAVES 2 DEAD, 35 INJURED&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;After the arrest, detectives asked for the public&apos;s help in identifying three other people &lt;a href=&quot;https://bouldercolorado.gov/news/two-men-shot-one-fatally-overnight-boulder-police-seek-publics-help&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;seen in video and photos&lt;/a&gt; from that night, including two males, one wearing an &quot;Art the Clown&quot; shirt and another in a red hoodie, and a female witness.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It’s unclear whether they will face charges.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;The investigation is ongoing. When and if there are additional arrests or charges, I will send out a news release,&quot; Waugh said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Shannon Carbone, the public information officer (PIO) for the Boulder County District Attorney’s Office, told Fox News Digital that prosecutors &quot;successfully argued in court Tuesday to have Perez held without bond.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Perez&apos;s preliminary hearing is scheduled for Feb. 10, 2027, according to the District Attorney&apos;s Office.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Colorado Public Defender’s Office declined to comment on the case. The university did not immediately respond to requests for comment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/us/teen-previously-convicted-shooting-accused-killing-pregnant-mom-4-spirit-halloween&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TEEN PREVIOUSLY CONVICTED IN SHOOTING ACCUSED OF KILLING PREGNANT MOM OF 4 INSIDE SPIRIT HALLOWEEN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;According to a &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/us/crime/police-and-law-enforcement&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Boulder police arrest affidavit&lt;/a&gt;, police first responded to a home off Marine Street around 9:58 p.m. on Halloween after receiving a noise complaint. Responding officers issued a nuisance-party citation, and hundreds of people left the gathering. Around 90 minutes later, at 11:28 p.m., officers returned after a call concerning gunshots fired.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Witnesses told authorities that Perez had been in the group of people that left, but he returned to the residence with six others. They were asked to leave, but Perez and his group allegedly became irate, leading to a scuffle in the living room and on the front porch. A witness said Perez appeared to be wearing a SWAT uniform and a &quot;Purge&quot; mask.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A resident at the home put Perez in a headlock, prompting Perez to allegedly pull out a gun and open fire, the affidavit stated.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;One witness told police he heard Perez threaten, &quot;Oh, I could shoot this place up.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/us/colorado-police-officer-killed-3-others-wounded-suspect-opens-fire-near-bus&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POLICE IDENTIFY AGENT KILLED AFTER SUSPECT OPENS FIRE NEAR COLORADO BUS, WOUNDS OTHER 3 OFFICERS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Perez shot Hanlon in the neck and another 19-year-old student in the leg. Hanlon died the following day at Boulder Community Health.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;I do not have any other updates on the second victim because of privacy. If that changes I will send out a news release,&quot; Waugh told Fox News Digital.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The arrest affidavit stated that Perez’s sister saw photos released by Boulder police and contacted them after recognizing her brother&apos;s clothes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;She then checked the family&apos;s &quot;Life360&quot; app, which tracked Perez arriving at the residence around the time of the shooting. The app also mapped his path following the shooting. Over the next several hours, Perez allegedly traveled through Westminster, Arvada, Keenesburg, and then back to Thornton.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;The defendant was arrested in Thornton. He is not a CU student and, contrary to some rumors, was not arrested on campus,&quot; Carbone told Fox News Digital.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/FoxTrueCrime&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FOLLOW THE FOX TRUE CRIME TEAM ON X&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;His sister told investigators that days before the shooting, Perez illegally purchased a 10mm Glock &quot;on the street&quot; and posted photos of the weapon on Instagram. She said he had replaced a revolver he &quot;threw in some bushes&quot; after accidentally shooting himself in the calf on Sept. 26.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The affidavit also noted that Perez and other people who accompanied him traveled in a newer red Audi sedan.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;When Perez picked his sister up from work, she got into the Audi and noticed a &quot;black purge looking mask&quot; on the floorboard. She also told police three people were in the vehicle with Perez.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/newsletters&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SIGN UP TO GET THE LATEST TRUE CRIME NEWS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Perez allegedly told his sister that they had been beaten up earlier at a party they attended, &quot;by four guys and his friends,&quot; the affidavit stated.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In addition to murder with extreme indifference, Perez faces first-degree assault and attempted first-degree murder charges, both with extreme indifference.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;For first degree murder, the only sentence allowed under law is life in prison without the possibility of parole. Additional charges will likely be filed,&quot; Carbone said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.colorado.edu/today/2026/11/02/university-statement-oct-31-shooting&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;CU Boulder identified&lt;/a&gt; Hanlon, of Pennsylvania, as a second-year media production student in its College of Communication, Media, Design and Information.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;It doesn&apos;t feel real. He was my best friend. He was always there. If I needed a shoulder to cry, he was there, to celebrate the biggest wins in life. He was just like an all-around, stand-up, great, just model citizen,&quot; Hanlon’s friend, Jack Anderson, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.denver7.com/news/local-news/in-your-community/boulder-county/he-was-who-i-aspired-to-be-in-life-he-was-that-person-roommates-remember-victim-of-boulder-shooting&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;told Denver’s ABC 7&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;I would say he was who I aspired to be in life. He was that person.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anyone with any information about the case is urged to contact Boulder police at 303-441-3333, or submit tips online at the police department’s &lt;a href=&quot;https://bouldercopd.evidence.com/axon/community-request/public/2610148&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;Evidence Submission Portal&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/Luca-Hanlon-killed-in-Boulder-Colorado.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">8f80e78c-66f0-5a3a-98b1-ead0da6613e0</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us/us-regions/west/colorado</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/crime</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us/crime/homicide</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us/education/college</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/us</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:00:31 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/food-drink/living-longer-start-3-foods-doctor-eats-every-day</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/food-drink/living-longer-start-3-foods-doctor-eats-every-day</guid> <title>Living longer may start with 3 foods a doctor eats every day</title>  <description>Coffee, cacao and raw honey are three foods a Florida physician says he consumes daily to support longevity and healthy aging, citing antioxidants and polyphenols.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;The secret to a longer, healthier life could start at the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/food-drink/recipes/meals/breakfast&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;breakfast&lt;/a&gt; table.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Dr. Mitch Ghen, a Boca Raton, Florida-based physician who has practiced functional medicine for more than 45 years, told Fox News Digital there are three &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/food-drink&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;foods and drinks&lt;/a&gt; he regularly consumes himself to support healthy aging: coffee, cacao and raw honey.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;I think these foods make a massive difference,&quot; Ghen said, adding that he incorporates them into his daily routine.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/health/longevity-doctor-reveals-what-matters-most-aging-well-beyond-pricey-biohacks&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;LONGEVITY DOCTOR REVEALS WHAT MATTERS MOST FOR AGING WELL, BEYOND PRICEY BIOHACKS&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ghen said he starts his mornings with &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/food-drink/drinks/coffee&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;coffee&lt;/a&gt; mixed with 100% cacao, while also consuming raw, unfiltered honey during the day.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Below are his three picks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ghen puts coffee at the top of his &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/health/healthy-living/longevity&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;longevity&lt;/a&gt; list, pointing to research that has associated coffee consumption with potential health benefits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/food-drink/food/studies&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;The studies&lt;/a&gt; suggest somewhere the sweet spot for coffee and longevity is between three and four cups a day,&quot; he said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ghen said he believes coffee can provide cardiovascular and immune benefits, in addition to the familiar boost in alertness.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/food-drink/coffee-lovers-can-take-heart-up-5-cups-day-appears-safe-most-adults-experts-say&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COFFEE LOVERS CAN TAKE HEART: UP TO 5 CUPS A DAY APPEARS SAFE FOR MOST ADULTS, EXPERTS SAY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;He personally opts for organic coffee and drinks it as part of his morning routine.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ghen gives his morning coffee an extra boost by adding 100% cacao that is high in polyphenols.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Polyphenols are naturally occurring plant compounds with antioxidant properties.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ghen said he typically recommends approximately a teaspoon to a tablespoon of cacao, depending on its polyphenol content.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;I think [the] combination tends to sit on top of each other and gives that person not only a great start in the morning, but certainly what I would call a good amount of antioxidants and polyphenols,&quot; he said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/food-drink/daily-coffee-habit-affect-brain-mood-unexpected-ways-study-finds#&amp;amp;_intcmp=fnc_category_category_main-content_article-list_2_2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;YOUR DAILY COFFEE HABIT MAY AFFECT YOUR BRAIN AND MOOD IN UNEXPECTED WAYS, STUDY FINDS&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ghen also pointed to research suggesting cacao may provide cardiovascular benefits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The third food on Ghen&apos;s list is raw, unfiltered, organic honey.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/lifestyle&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLICK HERE FOR MORE LIFESTYLE NEWS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ghen said honey may benefit the &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/food-drink/forget-yogurt-sauerkraut-5-gut-friendly-favorites-may-already-your-shelf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;gut microbiome&lt;/a&gt;, an area that has increasingly become a focus of research into overall health and aging.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;I love honey because I think it is one that helps longevity,&quot; he said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As for how much, Ghen recommends moderation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/newsletters?cmpid=fnfirstnl&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLICK HERE TO SIGN UP FOR OUR LIFESTYLE NEWSLETTER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;I think a tablespoon a day seems to be a reasonable amount without provoking too much spike in sugar,&quot; he said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;While Ghen incorporates all three foods into his own routine, he stressed that healthy aging is about more than adding individual &quot;superfoods&quot; to the diet.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;He said people should focus on sustainable eating habits and generally pointed to the &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/health/popular-diet-trend-boost-mental-health-older-adults-study-finds&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Mediterranean diet&lt;/a&gt; as a model.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For those who haven&apos;t always eaten well, it&apos;s never too late to make changes, Ghen said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/lifestyle/quizzes&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TEST YOURSELF WITH OUR LATEST LIFESTYLE QUIZ&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;The question that everyone should ask themselves is, quite seriously, is it about longevity, meaning a number, or is it the quality?&quot; he said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Quantity follows quality, so that&apos;s the key.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/drinking-coffee-aging-well.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">8bea2345-2992-53f0-8ab2-b195d2f56407</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/health/healthy-living/longevity</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/lifestyle</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/food-drink/food/healthy-foods</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/food-drink</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/lifestyle/food</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/food-drink/food</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/health/wellness</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/food-drink</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:00:43 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/us/harvard-scientist-pushes-back-nasa-chief-mystery-space-object-not-asteroid</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/us/harvard-scientist-pushes-back-nasa-chief-mystery-space-object-not-asteroid</guid> <title>Harvard scientist pushes back on NASA chief over mystery space object: &apos;It&apos;s not an asteroid&apos;</title>  <description>Avi Loeb challenges NASA&amp;apos;s Jared Isaacman, arguing 1998 KY26 is not an asteroid and could be a lost Soviet spacecraft from a failed Mars mission.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;A Harvard astrophysicist behind the theory that a mysterious object speeding through the solar system could actually be a lost Soviet spacecraft is pushing back on &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/science/air-and-space/nasa&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;NASA&lt;/a&gt;&apos;s top official, saying the object is &quot;not an asteroid.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Known as 1998 KY26, the roughly 36-foot-wide object is believed to be a &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/science/air-and-space/asteroids&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;near-Earth asteroid&lt;/a&gt; but is accelerating in a way gravity alone cannot explain. Harvard astrophysicist Avi Loeb and his colleagues have examined whether it could instead be Phobos 1, a Soviet spacecraft that stopped communicating while traveling to Mars in 1988.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;NASA Administrator Jared Isaacman weighed in on the mysterious object Thursday during an appearance on &quot;Fox &amp;amp; Friends.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/science/eiffel-tower-sized-asteroid-apophis-pass-closer-earth-many-satellites-2029-nasa-says&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EIFFEL TOWER-SIZED ASTEROID APOPHIS TO PASS CLOSER TO EARTH THAN MANY SATELLITES IN 2029, NASA SAYS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;I&apos;ve not seen any evidence to suggest this is...anything other than an asteroid,&quot; Isaacman said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Loeb challenged that assessment during an interview with Fox News Digital on Friday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/politics/harvard-astronomer-tapped-lead-white-house-ufo-council-says-us-government-baffled-what-they-are-seeing&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HARVARD ASTRONOMER TAPPED TO LEAD WHITE HOUSE UFO COUNCIL SAYS US GOVERNMENT &apos;BAFFLED BY WHAT THEY ARE SEEING&apos;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Well, first of all, it&apos;s not an asteroid because 1998 KY26 appears to have non-gravitational acceleration, meaning it&apos;s being pushed by some force other than gravity, and asteroids are just rocks,&quot; Loeb said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Scientists have been trying to explain what is causing the additional acceleration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/travel/scientists-discover-potentially-massive-dwarf-planet-candidate-hiding-beyond-pluto&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCIENTISTS DISCOVER POTENTIALLY MASSIVE DWARF PLANET CANDIDATE HIDING BEYOND PLUTO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;One theory has been that KY26 is a &quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/us/mysterious-object-moving-through-space-could-be-lost-soviet-probe-nasa-weighs-theory&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;dark comet&lt;/a&gt;,&quot; a rocky object behaving like a comet without producing a visible cloud or tail.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;New research from Georgia Tech has cast doubt on whether KY26 could retain enough ice to produce that effect, while other research has suggested pressure from sunlight and heat radiating from its surface could account for the acceleration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/tech/giant-robotic-claws-grab-dead-satellites-space&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GIANT ROBOTIC CLAWS WILL GRAB DEAD SATELLITES IN SPACE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Loeb told Fox News Digital that his team found KY26&apos;s trajectory closely resembles that of the failed Soviet mission and calculated that sunlight reflecting off Phobos 1 could produce a push consistent with the nongravitational acceleration observed in KY26.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;He also pointed to recent observations indicating the object is highly reflective and rotates about once every five minutes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/science/nasas-chandra-telescope-reveals-milky-ways-outer-reaches-may-stretch-farther-than-previously-known&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NASA&apos;S CHANDRA TELESCOPE REVEALS MILKY WAY&apos;S OUTER REACHES MAY STRETCH FARTHER THAN PREVIOUSLY KNOWN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The lack of a visible cometary tail or evidence of material escaping the object is central to Loeb&apos;s skepticism of the dark-comet explanation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;It could be a comet shedding some gas backward that is pushing it forward, but in that case we should have seen the gas,&quot; Loeb said. &quot;We should have seen the dust because for comets we see a tail and the dust particles are being pushed away from the sun by the solar radiation.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;We don&apos;t see a cometary tail. We don&apos;t see any evidence for outgassing around this object. That&apos;s the puzzle,&quot; he added.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Loeb compared the debate over how to classify KY26 to encountering an unfamiliar animal at a zoo.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/FoxTrueCrime&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FOLLOW THE FOX TRUE CRIME TEAM ON X&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;If you are an expert on zebras and you see an elephant, you would say the elephant is a zebra without stripes,&quot; Loeb said. &quot;But that&apos;s an oxymoron because it&apos;s a completely different animal.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;He also argued that scientists should be willing to consider explanations outside the familiar categories of asteroids and comets when observations do not neatly fit either one.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/politics/next-frontier-washington-grapples-its-latest-space-oddity&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE NEXT FRONTIER: WASHINGTON GRAPPLES WITH ITS LATEST SPACE ODDITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Innovation in science requires some imagination,&quot; Loeb said. &quot;It requires you to allow for the possibility that our knowledge is incomplete.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/newsletters&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SIGN UP TO GET THE LATEST TRUE CRIME NEWS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fox News Digital reached out to NASA for a response to Loeb&apos;s comments and asked whether Isaacman stands by his assessment of KY26.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/true-crime&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLICK HERE FOR MORE FROM THE FOX TRUE CRIME HUB&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Loeb acknowledged that his team&apos;s theory remains unproven, but said a definitive answer could come in 2031, when the Japan Aerospace Exploration Agency&apos;s &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/science/nasa-announces-three-new-moon-missions-agency-races-build-permanent-lunar-base-end-2026&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Hayabusa2 spacecraft&lt;/a&gt; is expected to rendezvous with KY26.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/tips&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SEND US A TIP&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Loeb predicts the encounter could show that scientists have been looking at a piece of Soviet space history rather than an unusual natural object.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/tips&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GOT A TIP?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;We predict that when they land on it, instead of seeing an iceberg, they will find the label ‘Made in the USSR,’&quot; Loeb said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://link.podtrac.com/cjdr_fnd_article&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LISTEN TO THE NEW &apos;CRIME &amp;amp; JUSTICE WITH DONNA ROTUNNO&apos; PODCAST&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Loeb also acknowledged that the 2031 encounter could settle the question once and for all.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/newsletters&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GET BREAKING NEWS BY EMAIL&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Asked whether the Phobos 1 theory would be completely over if Hayabusa2 reaches KY26 and finds a rock or piece of ice, Loeb didn&apos;t hesitate.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Yes,&quot; he said.&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/NASA-ASTEROID-ALERT-3.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">0a709c65-fba3-5085-80bc-4226ac22d150</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/science</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/science/air-and-space/nasa</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/science/air-and-space/mars</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/science/air-and-space/asteroids</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/science/air-and-space/spaceflight</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/science/air-and-space/astronomy</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/us</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:00:34 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/opinion/life-short-jerry-jones-makes-being-dallas-cowboys-fan-feel-endless</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/opinion/life-short-jerry-jones-makes-being-dallas-cowboys-fan-feel-endless</guid> <title>Life is short, but Jerry Jones makes being a Dallas Cowboys fan feel endless</title>  <description>Roger Staubach inspired a lifetime of Dallas Cowboys fandom, but Jerry Jones&amp;apos; 30-year Super Bowl drought is testing even the most loyal fans.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;Roger Staubach. That is the answer to the question: &quot;Why do you pull for the Dallas Cowboys? Yes, Mr. Staubach won the &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/sports/ncaa-fb&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Heisman Trophy&lt;/a&gt; before I was born. It is true I never watched him play a down of college football except in highlight films.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you don’t remember his first four years out of college playing professional football, do not feel badly. No one else does either, because he did not play professional football upon graduation from the Naval Academy. He served his country in uniform. We are now in an era where great baseball players skip college altogether, great basketball players are one and done, great football players leave for the draft as soon as they are eligible. Mr. Staubach was drafted in a different kind of way, and he opted for Vietnam when he may well have been able to stay stateside had he chosen to do so. First, it was Mr. Staubach and then Tom Landry, Jethro Pugh, Mel Renfro, Bob Lilly and Cliff Harris. I could name all the Cowboy players as a kid.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;I can still tell you where I was when Mr. Staubach threw that famous touchdown pass to Drew Pearson to beat the &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/sports/nfl/minnesota-vikings&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Minnesota Vikings&lt;/a&gt;. Yes, it is possible Drew Pearson pushed the defender down before he caught the ball, but let’s don’t get caught up in technicalities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/sports/cowboys-legend-digs-deep-teams-missing-fiber-thats-resulted-super-bowl-drought&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COWBOYS LEGEND DIGS DEEP INTO THE TEAM&apos;S MISSING &apos;FIBER&apos; THAT&apos;S RESULTED IN SUPER BOWL DROUGHT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Dallas is the only professional football team I have ever pulled for. Lately I have been wondering if life is too long to be a Cowboys fan. Our daughter loves the Cowboys so much she named her dog &quot;Dallas.&quot; Other family members gave up on Dallas when Jerry Jones bought the team and unceremoniously fired Tom Landry.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Yes, it was an egregious way to treat a legend, but perhaps not as egregious as his continued ownership of the franchise. That daughter who pulls so hard for Dallas has never seen them play in a Super Bowl. Not because she was doing something else or otherwise engaged on Super Bowl Sunday, but because Jerry Jones has managed something almost impossible. Dallas has not made the Super Bowl game in over 30 years. 25 different NFL franchises have played for a Super Bowl during this slough of despondance, but not Dallas.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you truly love something and value what is best for it, at what point do you do, as the old idiom commands, and &quot;set it free?&quot; Dallas has gone from winning three Super Bowls in four years and being a near constant threat to play for a division title to being unwatchable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It may well be the &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/sports/jerry-jones-open-co-owning-cowboys-mark-cuban-respect&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;most valuable franchise&lt;/a&gt; in all professional sports. Their budget is no less and probably more than any other NFL team and yet, under Jerry Jones’ leadership, they have hit rock bottom. The primary reason to watch these days is to see the new and creative ways they can blow leads or watch a defense that is apparently worried about being charged with assault and battery. [Free legal advice. It is not a battery to hit someone in a football game. The other team has consented to the touching.]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/cowboys-hire-longtime-nfl-coach-retirement-address-teams-brutal-defensive-start&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COWBOYS HIRE LONGTIME NFL COACH OUT OF RETIREMENT TO ADDRESS TEAM&apos;S BRUTAL DEFENSIVE START&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It isn’t bad luck in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/2026-nfl-draft-will-be-one-worst-sporting-events-year&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;NFL draft&lt;/a&gt;. Dallas drafts well. &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/micah-parsons-moves-closer-highly-anticipated-return-coach-matt-lafleur-gives-encouraging-update&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Micah Parsons&lt;/a&gt; literally fell into their laps. That was before they decided to draft the best defensive player in football, of course.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Dallas currently has a more than adequate quarterback and two of the best wide receivers in all of football. What they do not have is a good owner who knows anything about winning championships or even competing for them. Boston University has won a national championship in football just as recently as Dallas has played in a Super Bowl. [Note: Boston University discontinued its football program in 1997.]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/jerry-jones-no-succession-plan-cowboys-leadership-wont-here-toss-two-cents&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JERRY JONES HAS NO &apos;SUCCESSION PLAN&apos; FOR COWBOYS LEADERSHIP: &apos;JUST WON&apos;T BE HERE TO TOSS MY TWO CENTS IN&apos;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;I am too old to find another NFL team. I do not have 30 more years to wait for Jerry Jones to right this ship. The ship is not even headed in the right direction. Heck, it’s not even in the water at this point. I would buy them myself but for two things: they are not for sale, and I do not have 10 billion dollars (although I might could get Sean Hannity to loan it to me).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;I tell all the young people I know: &quot;Life is short, it goes quickly, relish every second.&quot; What I should tell them is watch Dallas play football. Life moves much more slowly. The penalties and defensive lapses mimic eternity. Mr. Jones, I, alongside many others, have pulled for Dallas all our lives. You are proving life may be too long.&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/10/1200/675/jerry-jones-dallas-cowboys-maracana-stadium.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">217ff002-9038-5aca-ab14-cb5404fc7bf6</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/opinion</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/nfl</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/nfl/dallas-cowboys</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/special/sponsored/american-legends</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/opinion</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:00:31 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/lifestyle/american-culture-quiz-test-yourself-fast-food-face-offs-oklahoma-origins</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/lifestyle/american-culture-quiz-test-yourself-fast-food-face-offs-oklahoma-origins</guid> <title>American Culture Quiz: Test yourself on fast-food face-offs and Oklahoma origins</title>  <description>The American Culture Quiz is a weekly test of our national traits, trends, history and people. This time, test your knowledge of fast-food face-offs, Oklahoma origins and a lot more.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;The American Culture Quiz is a weekly test of our unique national traits, trends, history and people — including the latest news, events and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/travel&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;sights and sounds&lt;/a&gt; of the United States.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This week&apos;s quiz highlights fast-food face-offs, Oklahoma origins — and a whole lot more.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Can you get all 8 questions right?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Give it a try and see how well you do!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/lifestyle&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;CLICK HERE FOR MORE LIFESTYLE STORIES&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;To try your hand at more quizzes from Fox News Digital, &lt;/i&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/lifestyle/fox-news-digital-news-quiz-may-1-2026&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;click here&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;i&gt; &lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;And to take our latest News Quiz — published every Friday — &lt;/i&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/lifestyle/fox-news-digital-news-quiz-november-13-2026&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;click here.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/updated-quiz-collage-1115.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">15b1b4af-9e2a-598e-8a42-f35dad974e2b</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/lifestyle/quizzes</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/lifestyle</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/travel</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/food-drink</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/health</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/entertainment</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/food-drink/food</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/lifestyle</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:00:53 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/politics/small-town-residents-cry-help-immigrant-influx-fueled-trucking-industry-unintended-consequences</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/politics/small-town-residents-cry-help-immigrant-influx-fueled-trucking-industry-unintended-consequences</guid> <title>Small town residents cry for help as immigrant influx fueled by trucking industry has unintended consequences</title>  <description>A Fox News Digital investigation reveals Hamilton Township&amp;apos;s freight fraud crackdown yielded 561 traffic stops and 36 arrests in southwest Ohio.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;This article is Part 3 of a Fox News Digital exclusive series investigating trucking fraud, public safety, and assimilation concerns in southwest Ohio. You can read &lt;/i&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/politics/uzbek-truck-driver-fatal-crash-exposed-troubling-fraud-trend-middle-america-chameleon-carriers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Part 1 here&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;i&gt; and &lt;/i&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/politics/alarming-fraud-trend-puts-small-town-mosque-industry-foreign-govt-ties-focus-our-motherland-now&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Part 2 here&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;i&gt;.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;OHIO - An influx of Uzbek immigrants and trucking companies, coupled with mounting concerns about roadway safety and alleged fraud, is fueling frustration in southwest &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/us/us-regions/midwest/ohio&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Ohio&lt;/a&gt;, where residents are speaking out about changes they say have left them feeling unsafe on their roads and increasingly uneasy in their own neighborhoods.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Jane, a resident of southwest Ohio, is one of many who have been affected by the Uzbek influx, which she says ultimately drove her out of a new home she purchased in the area after just 18 months of living there.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;I have literally been screaming about what has been going on for years, and I&apos;m like somebody needs to take notice of this,&quot; Jane told Fox News Digital.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Jane recounted repeated problems involving neighbors she identified as Uzbek, describing unsupervised children grabbing moving cars, climbing construction equipment, threatening to punch, kick or choke her dog, and taking her child&apos;s bicycle while ignoring demands to return it. She also described children urinating on neighbors’ vehicles, adults slaughtering chickens outdoors in view of her frightened child, and semi-truck cabs obstructing driveways.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/politics/working-class-americans-say-town-next-dearborn-theyve-had-enough&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WORKING-CLASS AMERICANS SAY THEIR TOWN IS THE NEXT DEARBORN — AND THEY&apos;VE HAD ENOUGH&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Jane described feeling &quot;incredibly uncomfortable&quot; encountering groups of roughly 15 men she identified as Uzbek gathered on the grass between neighboring homes while she was walking her dog.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;They all look at me like I have like 12 freaking heads, like I&apos;m the most disgusting person in the world,&quot; she said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Jane also described a situation where a group of Uzbek men showed up at her neighbor&apos;s door late at night carrying large bags before being told by the neighbor they had the wrong address. That neighbor then watched them go across the street into a garage and count cash that came from inside those bags.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;She estimated calling police roughly 20 times or more and said she felt authorities were unwilling or unable to intervene, leaving her family feeling they had little recourse but to leave. Jane was granted anonymity and is not using her real name due to fear for her family’s safety and possible retribution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/politics/trump-admin-investigating-75-truck-driver-schools-fraud-helping-non-citizens-get-licenses&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TRUMP ADMIN INVESTIGATING 75 TRUCK DRIVER SCHOOLS FOR FRAUD, HELPING NON-CITIZENS GET LICENSES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In nearby Middletown, Fox News Digital visited a site in mid-October that used to be a restaurant where GHOSTOPSUZ, a resident who has been flagging suspicious trucking companies and Uzbek influx to his followers anonymously online, used to frequent every Sunday after Mass with his family as a child.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Today, the building is abandoned and in disarray with smashed-out windows and no sign of life inside, but registered as the active headquarters of a trucking company, UAG Express, with over two dozen violations for infractions including vehicle maintenance, unsafe driving, suspended-CDL and an hours-of-service violation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;It&apos;s devastating, dude, I mean, it really is,&quot; GHOSTOPSUZ said as he walked around the dilapidated building that had multiple big rigs parked in the back but no sign of any recent activity. The location was recently &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/Wid_Lyman/status/2119879157308150114?a=RyMOF78_tmVcNTUTfGA&amp;amp;s=20&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;highlighted&lt;/a&gt; by Border Hawk News.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;My daughter plays competitive volleyball, so we&apos;re on these roads that we&apos;re sharing with these people that don&apos;t speak English, don&apos;t understand our laws, can&apos;t read our laws and frankly, I don&apos;t think they care, it’s quite obvious…and it doesn’t show respect for the community that you&apos;re in to do things like this.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/politics/out-control-unqualified-illegal-alien-truckers-endangering-kids-us-roads-insider-warns-just-madness&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OUT OF CONTROL, UNQUALIFIED ILLEGAL ALIEN TRUCKERS ENDANGERING KIDS ON US ROADS, INSIDER WARNS: ‘JUST MADNESS’&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fox News Digital reached out to UAG Express, owned by Aziz Ishanov, for comment but did not receive a response.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On Nov. 4, Fox News Digital attended a meeting where dozens of Hamilton Township residents expressed their concerns to the local trustees and told stories of first-hand experiences ranging from alleged trucking fraud to the mosque, to crowded schools, to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/crime&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;crime&lt;/a&gt; concerns related to the Uzbek community in the area.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;It has been a great place to grow up, now I&apos;m very concerned at this point with what we&apos;re learning about the fraud from these trucking companies, the Uzbek trucking companies, about the funds that they&apos;re using to build the mosque right now. I&apos;m just wondering, how did this get approved in the first place?&quot; One local resident asked.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Residents voiced concerns about a wide variety of issues including Uzbek men leering at women outside gyms, crowded schools, an unsupervised Uzbek child who recently drowned in a local pond, and Uzbek truck drivers offering money to women to get inside their trucks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;One resident said, &quot;Christian values are not compatible with Islamic values; they just simply aren&apos;t, and I don&apos;t like calling a people group out, especially as a Christian, that&apos;s very hard for me to do. But the facts are the facts, and we have to look at the facts. They are not here to assimilate; some are, I&apos;m sure. But I know how they operate.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;We are drowning,&quot; one resident said while discussing the crowded schools and students who can&apos;t speak English which has stretched resources thin. &quot;We are drowning here, our kids our suffering.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Local law enforcement has taken action on the trucking safety issue, and in the meeting, Hamilton Township Police Chief Quillan Short unveiled the data from a recent freight fraud crackdown that multiple local agencies coordinated between Oct. 19-23.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;That operation resulted in 561 traffic stops, 258 truck inspections, 423 citations and 73 vehicles being placed out of service. Authorities also placed 49 drivers out of service and made 36 arrests, including 31 on charges related to immigration-related offenses, according to data presented by Short.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hamilton Township Trustee Darryl Cordrey, in a statement to Fox News Digital, called the results of the crackdown &quot;staggering&quot; especially considering it only lasted 5 days.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Hamilton Township residents have every right to be concerned about unsafe commercial vehicles , unqualified drivers on our roads, and other criminal issues that have stemmed from the substantial increase in commercial trucking operations in Hamilton Township,&quot; Cordrey said. &quot;Our residents should not have to bear the consequences of failures in immigration policy and commercial trucking oversight.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cordrey added that the Biden administration&apos;s immigration policies have &quot;contributed to the broader problems we are now confronting&quot; and that he is &quot;fully committed&quot; to doing his part to resolve the issues working alongside local, state, and federal agencies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ohio &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/politics/house-of-representatives/republicans&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Republican&lt;/a&gt; state lawmaker Michelle Teska was present at the meeting as well and has taken action on the issue in the form of a &lt;a href=&quot;https://ohiohouse.gov/members/michelle-teska/news/teska-ohio-drivers-must-be-able-to-understand-english-149040#&amp;amp;_intcmp=fnc_politics_article_main-content_article-body_6_9&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;bill&lt;/a&gt; to strengthen commercial-driver licensing requirements, including a measure requiring driver examinations to be administered in English.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;We have a community that&apos;s being inundated with people from a certain area and how they got here is through the trucking industry, and they got here because, again, in the state of Ohio, you can get a CDL and a driver&apos;s license in 10 different languages,&quot; Teska told Fox News Digital, adding that she and the Hamilton Township trustees share the frustration and are doing what they can to address it despite many of the issues being rooted at the state and federal level.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The federal government has ramped up efforts to crack down on trucking fraud over the past year, and the Department of Transportation and Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration have mounted a sweeping crackdown on fraud and safety violations, placing roughly 34,000 drivers out of service for failing basic English-language proficiency requirements, revoking or canceling more than 31,000 illegally issued commercial driver’s licenses, and shutting down or purging nearly 10,000 noncompliant driving schools from the federal registry.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;This is a safety issue,&quot; Teska said. &quot;This is not a partisan issue in any way, shape, or form, but this is a safety issue, and you know we&apos;ve had a rape conviction, a federal human smuggling indictment, a fatal crash where a driver couldn&apos;t communicate with troopers without a translator, and every single one of those things was preventable.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Warren County Prosecutor David Fornshell previously told Fox News Digital that clearly &quot;there’s something going on&quot; within the Uzbek community in southwest Ohio that &quot;warrants at least awareness on the part of law enforcement.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;I would say hardly a week goes by where we don&apos;t have some felony case involving an Uzbek, it&apos;s pretty frequent at this point,&quot; Fornshell said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On Friday, the Islamic Center of Maineville, the mosque that has drawn the ire of some in the community, posted on its Telegram channel that it acknowledges the concerns and is hoping to work with the community to resolve them.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;On behalf of the Hamkor Uzbek Cincinnati Association, we recognize that some local residents have concerns and questions about our community. We believe that mutual respect, open communication, and understanding are the best ways to address these issues,&quot; the message said. &quot;Our Uzbek community is willing to listen to local residents, understand their concerns, clear up any misunderstandings, and work together to find practical solutions. We want to build trust, strengthen relationships, and promote unity between the Uzbek community and our neighbors. We believe that respectful dialogue and cooperation, rather than arguments and division, will help us move forward as one community.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Data from the 2024 Census show that roughly 1,500 people born in Uzbekistan live in Greater Cincinnati, while about 3,800 Uzbekistan-born residents live across Ohio. Uzbek community leaders say the actual population is significantly higher, estimating that roughly 4,000 Uzbek families live in southern Ohio, including U.S.-born children.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Our community was selected by the Uzbeks because they didn&apos;t think we would push back on their foreign influence,&quot; online researcher Nodawolf, a local resident who has been at the forefront of reporting on alleged trucking fraud over the past year, said via a statement read by an attendee at the trustees meeting. &quot;Here we are. We are here to say that our community will not be exploited for their monetary gain.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/politics/america-up-close&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;America Up Close&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt; is a Fox News Digital Politics series taking the country’s biggest political debates beyond Washington to uncover their real-world costs for the Americans living with the results.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/Broken-Glass-Trucks.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">720e0559-2f05-53b8-b5bb-d7c137fb51db</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/politics</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us/us-regions/midwest/ohio</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us/immigration/illegal-immigrants</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us/immigration/migrant-crime</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us/immigration/enforcement</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/news-events/fox-news-investigates</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/politics</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:00:51 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/us/ups-cargo-plane-copa-airlines-passenger-jet-collide-miami-airport-leaving-2-injured</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/us/ups-cargo-plane-copa-airlines-passenger-jet-collide-miami-airport-leaving-2-injured</guid> <title>UPS cargo plane, Copa Airlines passenger jet collide at Miami airport, leaving 2 injured</title>  <description>A UPS Airlines cargo plane and a Copa Airlines passenger jet collided on the ground at Miami International Airport on Saturday night, leaving two people with minor injuries.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;A UPS cargo plane and a Copa Airlines passenger jet collided on the ground at &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/us/miami&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Miami International Airport&lt;/a&gt; Saturday night, leaving two people with minor injuries, airport officials confirmed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) said the wingtip of a Copa Airlines Boeing 737 struck the nose of a UPS Boeing 767 while both aircraft were taxiing around 9 p.m. local time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Air traffic controllers had instructed the UPS crew to give way to the Copa Airlines flight, which was heading to its gate after landing, while the UPS cargo plane was preparing to depart for Bogotá, Colombia, according to the FAA.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The agency said it is investigating the collision.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/us/amazon-cargo-jet-overruns-miami-airport-runway-triggering-massive-emergency-response&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AMAZON CARGO PLANE OVERRUNS MIAMI AIRPORT RUNWAY AND STRIKES &apos;MULTIPLE&apos; VEHICLES; 5 DEAD, 5 INJURED&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;At approximately 9:15 p.m., an arriving aircraft and a departing aircraft made contact with each other at the intersection of two taxiways,&quot; Greg Chin, communications director for the Miami-Dade Aviation Department, said in a statement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Flights are being directed to other taxiways, so there is no impact to airport operations at this time. Two patients were treated on the scene by Miami-Dade Fire Rescue for minor injuries and did not require medical transport,&quot; Chin added.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/us/air-traffic-audio-captures-jetblue-pilot-alerting-controllers-collided-drone&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Air traffic control audio&lt;/a&gt; reviewed by Fox News Digital captured an exchange between pilots and a controller following the collision.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A pilot aboard the Copa Airlines flight was heard saying, &quot;Somebody just hit us.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/us/ntsb-report-details-controller-decision-tech-failures-led-deadly-runway-collision&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NTSB REPORT DETAILS HOW CONTROLLER DECISION AND TECH FAILURES LED TO DEADLY RUNWAY COLLISION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;UPS 358, did you hit that aircraft?&quot; an air traffic controller asked.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Yeah, we went too far and he clipped us with his wing,&quot; the UPS pilot responded.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Copa Airlines said Flight CM427, arriving from Panama City, Panama, was carrying 166 passengers and six crew members when the collision occurred.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The airline said the Boeing 737&apos;s left wingtip was involved in the collision with the cargo plane while both aircraft were taxiing.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;All passengers disembarked at the terminal, with two receiving treatment for apparent minor injuries, the airline added.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;UPS Airlines also acknowledged the incident in a statement posted on X.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;We are aware of an incident involving one of our aircraft on the ground in Miami,&quot; the company said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/travel/4-critical-travel-issues-those-still-scrambling-after-faa-nationwide-ground-stop&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4 CRITICAL TRAVEL ISSUES FOR THOSE DELAYED AND DISRUPTED BY FAA NATIONWIDE GROUND STOP&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Our crew is safe, and we are committed to working with authorities to determine what happened. The safety of our employees and the public is our highest priority.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The collision came as U.S. airports continued recovering from Friday&apos;s nationwide Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) ground stop, which disrupted thousands of flights after radar and &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/media/former-top-faa-official-warns-48-hour-recovery-aging-tech-overwhelmed-ground-stop&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;communications systems experienced instability&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Transportation Secretary &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/politics/duffy-unleashes-buttigieg-swipe-over-admin-has-accomplished-more-sloth&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Sean Duffy&lt;/a&gt; said Saturday that air traffic control communications had returned to full operations, while FAA Administrator Bryan Bedford said airlines expected to restore their full schedules by the end of Sunday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fox News Digital has reached out to UPS, Copa Airlines and the FAA for additional comment.&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/ups-copa-airlines-miami-airport-collision.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">3bd87d22-8555-50f5-b826-96fb3cfe954d</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us/us-regions/southeast/florida</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us/miami</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/travel/general/airlines</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/travel/general/airports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/science/air-and-space</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/us</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:43:15 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/arch-manning-overcomes-sloppy-performance-clutch-td-pass-lift-texas-lsu-crucial-matchup</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/arch-manning-overcomes-sloppy-performance-clutch-td-pass-lift-texas-lsu-crucial-matchup</guid> <title>Arch Manning turns Death Valley into LSU’s funeral as Texas buries Lane Kiffin’s CFP hopes</title>  <description>Lane Kiffin&amp;apos;s $40 million LSU roster watched Arch Manning deliver a late touchdown pass to Raleek Brown that ended the Tigers&amp;apos; playoff dreams.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;BATON ROUGE, La. — Turns out, the Texas Longhorns had one last drive left in them, on a night when nothing was going &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/person/arch-manning&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Arch Manning&apos;s&lt;/a&gt; way.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;What we witnessed on Saturday night inside Tiger Stadium will be remembered for quite some time, by both Texas and &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/sports/ncaa/lsu-tigers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;LSU&lt;/a&gt; fans.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;What started as a party for the Tiger faithful turned into a funeral for the LSU 2026 season that will leave folks in Louisiana wondering how they could give this one away to the Longhorns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/lsu-head-coach-lane-kiffin-making-same-mistake-predecessor-suffer-same-fate&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LSU HEAD COACH LANE KIFFIN IS MAKING THE SAME MISTAKE HIS PREDECESSOR DID, WILL HE SUFFER THE SAME FATE?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The pressure entering this one was heavy on both sides. Texas could not afford another loss and feel totally safe in making the postseason, while a fourth loss for LSU would put an end to their CFP hopes, even if they were already hanging by a thread.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Was there some hesitation among LSU fans to get overly excited about this one? If you were wondering why, the final drive of this game all but proved their point that &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/lane-kiffin-staring-down-disastrous-year-one-offseason-pleas-patience-fall-deaf-ears&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Lane Kiffin&lt;/a&gt; is the same guy who could not win the big game at Ole Miss, and now as head coach of the Tigers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Maybe that&apos;s because Sam Leavitt had three interceptions through three quarters tonight, and it&apos;s hard to trust this LSU offense at times. It wasn’t if the other side was any better though, with Arch Manning throwing three of his own.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLICK HERE FOR MORE OUTKICK SPORTS COVERAGE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Why not? This is LSU football we&apos;re talking about here, with a head coach that has spent over $40 million on its roster this season. You bet that Kiffin and his staff felt the pressure in the week leading up to this one, and rightfully so.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This was a game in which both teams could not afford to lose, even though that swayed more in the direction of LSU given their three losses.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As day turned into night, the craziness began for both teams. Multiple interceptions, special teams blunders and some interesting play calling on each side of the field.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;But, it was Arch Manning that had the ball with just over two minutes remaining in a game that set offenses back years up until the final drive of the game. If there’s one thing we’ve learned about the Texas Longhorns this season, it’s that we can’t put anything past them.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A 12-play, 58-yard drive would seal the deal for a Texas team that had one last chance to pull off a miracle in Baton Rouge.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Were you expecting anything different?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/newsletters&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;SIGN UP FOR THE DAILY OUTKICK NEWSLETTER&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Arch Manning hit Raleek Brown on a swing pass that caught the LSU defense off guard, and Brown fought his way into the end zone to secure Texas’ 22-21 win, drawing a roar from a Texas crowd that had essentially taken over the southern end of Tiger Stadium.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Just when you thought the Longhorns were done, the defense gave this team one last chance to pull off what many will remember as one of the best moments of Arch Manning&apos;s college career. Let me be clear that this Texas offense looked putrid at times, getting torched along the line of scrimmage, while Manning would end the game with three interceptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;But, all it took was one legendary drive for a quarterback that will be remembered for a number of inconsistencies in college.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On Saturday night, none of that mattered when Manning grabbed &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/steve-sarkisian-face-college-footballs-hardest-call-arch-manning-invokes-much-higher-stakes&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Steve Sarkisian&lt;/a&gt; during the post-game interview with ESPN. His interceptions will be remembered by those who cover him on a daily basis, but the touchdown pass will live on forever in Texas lore.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As Sarkisian and Manning headed towards the Texas end zone to greet the fans who made the chaotic trip to Baton Rouge, you could once again see what once again looked like disbelief come across the face of the starting quarterback.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Not that Arch thought he couldn’t do it. But more so, the fact that so many things were not going his way leading up to that final drive.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Holy sh-t,&quot; Manning proclaimed as he bent over in the end zone during the postgame celebration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;That was incredible.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On the other hand, LSU finds itself done with any talk of playing in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/college-football-playoff-rankings-miami-takes-top-spot-indiana-cracks-top-five-first-official-release&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;college football playoff&lt;/a&gt;. A roster worth over $40 million will now be sitting at home while others fight for a national championship, to the dismay of Tiger fans that bought into the words of their head coach.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fool you once, shame on you. Fool you four times, you&apos;re just out of luck.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Arch Manning delivered a dagger to his home state on Saturday night, just when those around the college football community thought the Longhorns were done in Baton Rouge.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We got the ending we deserved after sitting through that offensive disaster for nearly an entire game.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For the Texas Longhorns, the season continues and a run towards the college football playoff might have started weeks ago.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;But tonight inside Tiger Stadium, Arch Manning and Steve Sarkisian dialed up a drive that will be remembered forever in Austin.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;And, it was the Tigers that brought out another side of a Manning that we have not seen before.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/steve-sarkisian-faces-brutal-arch-manning-decision-texas-season-begins-slip-away-amid-losses&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Texas&apos; season&lt;/a&gt; will more than likely continue into late December.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lane Kiffin is going to have a hard time answering this one at the local quarterback club once this season finally ends.&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/archmanninglsu1.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">8d7e855f-5035-5c7d-a981-d14e319914d5</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa-fb</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/person/arch-manning</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa/texas-longhorns</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa/lsu-tigers</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/university</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/betting</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:57:46 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/us/masked-dirt-bike-riders-swarm-suv-brazen-nyc-street-attack-sparking-police-crackdown</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/us/masked-dirt-bike-riders-swarm-suv-brazen-nyc-street-attack-sparking-police-crackdown</guid> <title>Masked dirt bike riders swarm SUV in brazen NYC street attack, sparking police crackdown</title>  <description>Video captures masked dirt bike riders swarming and attacking an SUV on a busy Staten Island street as the NYPD warns that arrests are near.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/us/new-york-city&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;New York City&lt;/a&gt; officials are warning a group of masked dirt bike riders that arrests could be imminent after video captured a chaotic confrontation in which several riders surrounded and attacked a vehicle on a busy Staten Island street.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The crackdown follows a Wednesday incident on Richmond Avenue in Staten Island&apos;s Bulls Head neighborhood, where video showed several masked riders swarming a white SUV stopped at a traffic light.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In the video obtained by Fox News Digital, several individuals appeared to kick and strike the vehicle, while another appeared to throw an object at it. As the driver attempted to leave, the SUV appeared to run over a dirt bike that had been positioned in front of the vehicle.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/us/watch-ebike-teen-takeover-swarms-downtown-city-streets-blocking-traffic-leading-charges&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WATCH: E-BIKE TEEN TAKEOVER SWARMS DOWNTOWN CITY STREETS BLOCKING TRAFFIC, LEADING TO CHARGES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;During a news conference Thursday, NYPD Assistant Chief John Buttacavoli warned those involved that police were gathering intelligence and working to identify the suspects.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;We know who you are, and you will be getting a knock on your door very soon,&quot; Buttacavoli said, emphasizing that the behavior had escalated from a quality-of-life concern into criminal activity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;It stops here. We&apos;re taking action,&quot; he added.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Staten Island District Attorney Michael McMahon also condemned the riders, accusing them of intimidating motorists and putting innocent people at risk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/us/video-shows-bridge-turn-burnout-bonanza-stunt-happy-takeover-police-swoop-cuff-road-rebels&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;VIDEO SHOWS BRIDGE TURN INTO BURNOUT BONANZA IN STUNT-HAPPY TAKEOVER – POLICE SWOOP IN TO CUFF ROAD REBELS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Like a plague of locusts, they descend upon drivers who are just going about their business here on Staten Island,&quot; McMahon said. &quot;They&apos;re jackals, they&apos;re teenage terrorists, and it&apos;s not going to be tolerated here in our borough.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;McMahon called the behavior &quot;simply outrageous,&quot; adding that no one had been seriously injured, based on the information available to officials.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Wednesday&apos;s incident was part of a broader pattern of &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/us/boston-cop-pelted-mob-dirt-bike-suspect-escapes-wild-viral-video-he-all-alone&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;dangerous behavior involving motorized bikes&lt;/a&gt;, according to Staten Island Borough President Vito Fossella.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fossella described the riders as a &quot;bunch of punks who are literally terrorizing drivers&quot; as motorists went about their daily routines.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Enough. This game is over,&quot; Fossella said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The borough president also warned parents that their children were putting innocent motorists at risk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/us/cities-fearing-halloween-mayhem-put-teens-notice-announce-curfews-crackdowns-violent-takeovers&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CITIES FEARING HALLOWEEN MAYHEM PUT TEENS ON NOTICE, ANNOUNCE CURFEWS AND CRACKDOWNS AFTER VIOLENT TAKEOVERS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Your kid is terrorizing innocent people when they&apos;re just going about their business. It&apos;s wrong, and it needs to stop,&quot; Fossella said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;McMahon warned that parents could face legal or financial consequences if their children use illegal motorized vehicles to intimidate or injure others, including potential civil liability if someone is hurt.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Parents also must take responsibility for their children,&quot; McMahon&apos;s office said in a separate statement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Police have assembled a task force to address the problem and will continue &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/us/west-coast-state-sheriffs-bait-bike-sting-snares-dozens-alleged-thieves-just-months&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;confiscating illegally operated motorized bikes&lt;/a&gt;, according to Buttacavoli. He said officers had already identified several individuals and seized numerous bikes this year.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/us/grinning-suspect-cuffed-alleged-fiery-street-takeover-drag-race-caught-camera&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GRINNING SUSPECT CUFFED AFTER ALLEGED FIERY STREET TAKEOVER, DRAG RACE CAUGHT ON CAMERA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The NYPD also reminded residents that certain motorized vehicles must be registered, insured and operated by licensed drivers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;State Assemblyman Mike Reilly, R-Staten Island, said he plans to introduce legislation in January that would hold &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/politics/blue-state-school-district-accused-defying-supreme-court-hiding-gender-transitions-parents&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;parents financially responsible&lt;/a&gt; for minors caught recklessly operating certain motorized vehicles, according to the New York Post.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The proposal would impose fines ranging from $250 to $1,500, the paper reported.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The incident remains under investigation, and no arrests have been announced.&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/staten-island-dirt-bike-riders-attack-suv.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">57ac5593-1f59-5c3a-a0d8-709b1b26ce95</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/crime</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us/new-york-city</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us/us-regions/northeast/new-york</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/politics/elections/local</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us/crime/police-and-law-enforcement</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/shows/cops</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/us</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:55:51 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/benches-clear-chaotic-postgame-brawl-louisville-cardinals-top-north-carolina-tar-heels</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/benches-clear-chaotic-postgame-brawl-louisville-cardinals-top-north-carolina-tar-heels</guid> <title>Benches clear in chaotic postgame brawl after Louisville Cardinals top North Carolina Tar Heels</title>  <description>A bench-clearing brawl erupted after Louisville&amp;apos;s late interception sealed a 16-14 college football win over Bill Belichick&amp;apos;s North Carolina.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/sports/ncaa/louisville-cardinals&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Louisville Cardinals&lt;/a&gt; managed to beat the North Carolina Tar Heels 16-14 after a late interception ended UNC&apos;s hopes of taking the lead.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;While that sounds exciting, it&apos;s no match for the all-out brawl that erupted as the clock wound down to zero.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;With just over a minute to go, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/sports/ncaa/north-carolina-tar-heels&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;UNC&apos;s&lt;/a&gt; Travis Burgess seemed to have thrown a pass that would move the Tar Heels close to midfield; however, it wound up in the arms of a Cardinal.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/rams-offensive-lineman-punches-bills-linebacker-after-thrilling-game-tempers-got-flared&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RAMS OFFENSIVE LINEMAN PUNCHES BILLS LINEBACKER AFTER THRILLING GAME: &apos;TEMPERS GOT FLARED&apos;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bummer. That&apos;s it. Game over. Everyone can leave. Nothing else to see.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Well, any fans who did stick around saw something wild. As the Cardinals took a knee for the final time, tempers started flaring.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Then they kept flaring, and really never stopped.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/florida-high-school-football-game-erupts-violent-brawl-involving-players-coaches-final-whistle&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;The benches cleared&lt;/a&gt;, and chaos ensued.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We also got one of my favorite things, which is officials trying to break up a brawl by blowing their whistles and &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/nfl-refs-set-all-time-record-flags-season-changing-outcome-games&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;throwing flags&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Seriously? In that melee, do you really think whistling away like a London Bobby is going to do anything?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/sec-head-greg-sankey-blasts-announcers-criticizing-poor-officiating-texas-missouri-unacceptable&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SEC HEAD GREG SANKEY BLASTS ANNOUNCERS FOR CRITICIZING POOR OFFICIATING IN TEXAS-MISSOURI: &apos;UNACCEPTABLE&apos;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Now you don&apos;t just have a brawl on your hands. You have a brawl, a total racket &lt;em&gt;and &lt;/em&gt;a bunch of flags you&apos;ve got to go and pick up.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;So, did any of that improve the situation in any measurable way?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;No. No, it did not.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Of course, with that much mayhem, there&apos;s not much the officiating can do (or would want to do), and it will be interesting to see if there&apos;s any supplemental discipline coming.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Tar Heels likely don’t need any, because they’re probably in for a rough few days.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It was a bad night on several fronts for Bill Belichick&apos;s boys. Something tells me it won&apos;t be a fun week as the 5-5 Tar Heels prepare to take on Virginia next weekend.&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/unc-louisville-brawl.png?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/png\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">0c506c2d-e228-5cc8-832e-c2bf2a587015</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa-fb</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa/louisville-cardinals</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa/north-carolina-tar-heels</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:42:25 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/kenneth-walker-iii-out-against-nfl-rushing-leader-bijan-robinson-falcons-patrick-mahomes-off-injury-report</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/kenneth-walker-iii-out-against-nfl-rushing-leader-bijan-robinson-falcons-patrick-mahomes-off-injury-report</guid> <title>Kenneth Walker III out against NFL rushing leader Bijan Robinson&apos;s Falcons, Patrick Mahomes off injury report</title>  <description>Kenneth Walker III was ruled out with a groin injury, leaving rookie Emmett Johnson to lead the Kansas City Chiefs&amp;apos; rushing attack on Sunday.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;The Chiefs will be without one of their biggest offensive threats when they visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/sports/nfl/atlanta-falcons&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;the Falcons&lt;/a&gt; on Sunday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kenneth Walker III, the NFL’s second-leading rusher, was ruled out Saturday with a groin injury and will miss his first game since joining &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/sports/nfl/kansas-city-chiefs&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Kansas City.&lt;/a&gt; Rookie running back Emmett Johnson will step in for Walker.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The matchup was set to showcase the league’s top two rushers. Atlanta’s Bijan Robinson leads the NFL with 880 rushing yards, just eight ahead of Walker’s 872. Walker has also caught 22 passes for 172 yards and four touchdowns, while Robinson has added 250 receiving yards.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLICK HERE FOR MORE OUTKICK SPORTS COVERAGE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Walker had been listed as questionable on the injury report after tweaking his groin during Thursday’s practice. Chiefs coach Andy Reid said the team would monitor his progress over the next couple of days.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/chiefs-kenneth-walker-runs-wild-bo-nix-melts-down-kansas-city-obliterates-broncos-mnf-blowout&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CHIEFS&apos; NEW STUD KENNETH WALKER RUNS WILD, BO NIX MELTS DOWN AS KANSAS CITY OBLITERATES BRONCOS IN MNF BLOWOUT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Johnson has played well when given a chance this season, though. The overlooked fifth-round pick out of Nebraska has run 26 times for 111 yards and a touchdown, and he’s caught 14 passes for 237 yards and another score.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;He’s going to play anyway, whether Ken’s there or not,&quot; Reid said Friday. &quot;Everybody has confidence in him.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Chiefs’ bigger problem is the lack of depth behind Johnson. Brashard Smith went on injured reserve with a hamstring injury Oct. 24, while Ott is questionable for Sunday’s game in Atlanta with a sore hamstring. He carried three times for 19 yards in mop-up duty during last week’s blowout win over the Jets.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Chiefs also received good news on the injury front. Two-time NFL MVP Patrick Mahomes was listed as a full participant throughout the week and carries no injury designation for Sunday’s game.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mahomes was able to bounce back after taking a hard hit to his right arm during last week’s 35-12 &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/patrick-mahomes-suffers-apparent-elbow-injury-throwing-arm-returns-face-new-york-jets&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;win over the Jets.&lt;/a&gt; An MRI taken afterward showed no major injury to his right elbow, NFL Network reported.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Chiefs were flying to Atlanta on Saturday, and they did not expect any changes to their flight plan following the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/faa-ground-stop-leaves-college-football-teams-stranded-eve-crucial-saturday-showdowns&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Federal Aviation Administration’s ground stoppage&lt;/a&gt; a day earlier. Standout defensive tackle Chris Jones was not traveling with the team for personal reasons, but the Chiefs said he would join the team in Atlanta and he carried no game designation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;The Associated Press contributed to this report.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/Kansas-City-Kenneth-Walker-III.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">bd683711-4d26-5975-b5fa-63c79fe71838</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/nfl/kansas-city-chiefs</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/nfl/atlanta-falcons</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/nfl</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/topic/trending-news</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/betting</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:10:17 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/georgia-football-three-star-recruit-marcellus-young-casario-dies-after-medical-emergency-high-school-says</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/georgia-football-three-star-recruit-marcellus-young-casario-dies-after-medical-emergency-high-school-says</guid> <title>Georgia football three-star recruit Marcellus Young Casario dies after &apos;medical emergency,&apos; high school says</title>  <description>Marcellus Young Casario, a Georgia Bulldogs defensive lineman commit, died after a sudden medical emergency at his Rabun Gap boarding school.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/sports/ncaa-fb&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;college football&lt;/a&gt; community is mourning the death of a promising young player.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Marcellus Young Casario, 18, died Friday after what his &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/us/education/high-school&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;high school&lt;/a&gt; described as a &quot;sudden medical emergency.&quot; Casario was rated a three-star recruit and played defensive line.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Casario was from Canada and a senior at Rabun Gap-Nacoochee School, a boarding school in Georgia located roughly 114 miles northeast of Atlanta. The school announced Friday that an unidentified student had died and later postponed a state playoff game scheduled for that night.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLICK HERE FOR MORE OUTKICK SPORTS COVERAGE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rabun Gap-Nacoochee School said it followed its emergency response protocols after a boarding student experienced a medical incident Friday morning.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;The boarding student had a medical incident this morning,&quot; the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/p/DfsyDrAzfmA/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;school said in a statement&lt;/a&gt; post to social media. &quot;Rabun Gap immediately followed our emergency response protocols, and local emergency personnel responded, transferring the student to the hospital.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Casario was later identified as the student. Other details about what led to Friday’s medical emergency were not immediately available.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Casario started playing organized football at an independent boarding school in Aurora, Ontario. In 2025 and shortly before his junior season kicked off, Casario transferred to Rabun Gap-Nacoochee.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/division-ii-running-back-pronounced-dead-after-medical-emergency-teams-season-opener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DIVISION-II RUNNING BACK PRONOUNCED DEAD AFTER MEDICAL EMERGENCY IN TEAM&apos;S SEASON OPENER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;He did see his dreams of receiving a college football scholarship come true. After visiting Georgia and Michigan State, among other schools, Casario landed offers from Georgia, Miami and Virginia Tech before committing to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/sports/ncaa/georgia-bulldogs&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;the Bulldogs&lt;/a&gt; on June 15.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;He was everything a coach wants in a player,&quot; Rabun Gap-Nacoochee football coach Derek White said in a statement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;[Marcellus] truly embodied our mission to &apos;love one another.&apos; He was known for his relentless dedication, and his journey as a student-athlete was marked by hard work and true brotherhood with his teammates.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;ESPN ranked Casario as the No. 49 defensive end in the nation.&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2025/12/931/523/georgia-football-helmets.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">40ede76b-5b6f-5cee-b78e-fad1dbeb3a91</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa/georgia-bulldogs</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa-fb</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/entertainment/events/departed</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:50:34 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/florida-stuns-kentucky-21-14-gators-pull-off-yet-another-upset-win-up-down-season</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/florida-stuns-kentucky-21-14-gators-pull-off-yet-another-upset-win-up-down-season</guid> <title>Florida stuns Kentucky 21-14 as Gators pull off yet another upset win in up-and-down season</title>  <description>Florida Gators pulled off their third upset of a ranked opponent this season, stunning No. 11 Kentucky 21-14 with a gutsy two-point conversion.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;When you&apos;re the No. 11 team in the nation and battling for a crack at the &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/sports/ncaa-fb&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;College Football Playoff&lt;/a&gt; like the Kentucky Wildcats, you&apos;d normally be licking your chops at the prospect of a 5-4 team paying you a visit.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;However, that team happened to be the &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/sports/ncaa/florida-gators&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Florida Gators&lt;/a&gt;. They&apos;ve been struggling as of late, but still have a pair of shocking upset wins on their resume this season, taking down both Ole Miss and Texas.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;So, there was nothing they&apos;d like more than playing spoiler and maybe getting their season back on track.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/current-three-loss-team-most-dangerous-college-football-playoff&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHICH CURRENT THREE-LOSS TEAM WOULD BE THE MOST DANGEROUS IN THIS YEAR&apos;S COLLEGE FOOTBALL PLAYOFF?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;But before we get to the game, we must take a moment to acknowledge &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/sports/ncaa/kentucky-wildcats&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Kentucky&apos;s&lt;/a&gt; drone show.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Drones are way better than fireworks. I will die on that hill.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anyway, it took a while for anyone to put points on the board. Kentucky struck first when QB Kenny Minchey found running back CJ Baxter for a touchdown with under two minutes to go in the first quarter.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In the second quarter, Florida got rid of its goose egg thanks to an offensive holding penalty in the end zone, which resulted in a safety.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As rough as it has been for Florida, they had to have been happy heading to the locker room at halftime trailing just 7-2.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;And what they had to have liked even more was scoring a touchdown in the third quarter to take their first lead in several weeks. Running back Jadan Baugh took matters into his own hands and punched it into the end zone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kentucky answered back with a Kenny Minchey 1-yard keeper for a touchdown, while the Gators settled for a field goal to make it 14-13 going into the fourth quarter.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gators quarterback Aaron Philo led the team on an impressive 14-play drive that ended with him using his legs to retake the lead.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Jon Sumrall took a bit of a gamble by keeping his offense on the field for a two-point conversion attempt, and that proved to be a good call. Phylo rolled out and lobbed a pass to a wide-open Dallas Wilson to extend the lead to 21-14.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;But, of course, what would this be without a little drama?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Florida decided to go for it on 4th-and-1 just past midfield. A first down would&apos;ve ended the game as Kentucky was out of timeouts. However, the Wildcats&apos; defense did their job and stopped the Gators about an inch short.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;That meant the offense got one more crack at it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Unfortunately, for Will Stein&apos;s offense, they couldn&apos;t get anything going. Minchey threw three straight incomplete passes, then left the offense on the field to go for it on 4th-and-10.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Gators might be the definition of feast or famine this season. That&apos;s a third &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/florida-drops-impressive-offensive-performance-pull-off-massive-win-no-4-ole-miss&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;upset win over a ranked opponent&lt;/a&gt;... and they&apos;re still 6-4 on the year.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/college-football-playoff-rankings-georgia-rises-no-1-notre-dame-cracks-top-5-big-win-miami&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COLLEGE FOOTBALL PLAYOFF RANKINGS: GEORGIA RISE TO NO. 1, NOTRE DAME CRACKS TOP 5 AFTER BIG WIN OVER MIAMI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Talk about some ups and downs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The loss puts a huge dent in Kentucky&apos;s playoff hopes. They&apos;ll face Missouri next week, while Florida heads back to the Swamp to take on Vanderbilt.&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/florida-kentucky-2.png?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/png\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">7f0cfbda-8b26-5acc-8312-222e1b741d56</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa-fb</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa/florida-gators</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa/kentucky-wildcats</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/betting</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:33:26 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/federal-judge-blocks-trumps-renovations-dc-golf-course-hours-before-closure</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/federal-judge-blocks-trumps-renovations-dc-golf-course-hours-before-closure</guid> <title>Federal judge blocks Trump&apos;s renovations of DC golf course hours before its closure</title>  <description>A federal judge cited Donald Trump&amp;apos;s Truth Social posts as key evidence when issuing a temporary restraining order on the East Potomac renovation.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;A federal judge issued a temporary restraining order Saturday to delay closing a D.C.-area golf course amid President &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/person/donald-trump&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Donald Trump&lt;/a&gt;&apos;s push to have the course renovated.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;U.S. District Judge Ana Reyes issued the two-week delay before the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/sports/golf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;East Potomac Golf Links&lt;/a&gt; was due to close Sunday for 15 months.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The course sits on federally owned land at East Potomac Park and has been part of Washington&apos;s public golf scene for more than a century. Trump announced in May the course would undergo a &quot;historic renovation&quot; that would prepare it to host major professional golf events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLICK HERE FOR MORE OUTKICK SPORTS COVERAGE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The plaintiffs argue that Trump&apos;s plan would change the character of the accessible golf course and make it unaffordable, something the president denies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The White House did not immediately respond to a request for comment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Trump has dubbed the course &quot;Trash Island,&quot; doing so as recently on Saturday in a Truth Social post in which he said it is the &quot;worst&quot; course in the world.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Trump said the conditions of the course are &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/trump-takes-parting-shot-dc-golf-course-conditions-one-day-before-major-overhaul-begins&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&quot;very dangerous,&quot;&lt;/a&gt; adding pictures of what appears to be the course in poor shape.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;The Fairways are far too close together. When you walk down the corridors of Trash Island, you don’t hear the sound of the running Potomac, all you hear is the sound of people screaming, &apos;FORE!&apos;,&quot; Trump wrote.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Trump has posted about the course in the past. Reyes in her ruling Saturday noted that Trump&apos;s posts presented a problem for the government.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/newsletters&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SIGN UP FOR THE DAILY OUTKICK NEWSLETTER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;They indicate that the Washington National Plan is final and that [National Park Service] will close the Park to implement it,&quot; she wrote. &quot;Both points favor granting Plaintiffs’ motion for another temporary restraining order.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The park’s redevelopment is one of multiple projects in the nation&apos;s capital that Trump has championed to remake the city. They include a large memorial arch, a White House ballroom and the John F. Kennedy Center for the Performing Arts, among others.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reyes, who was nominated to the court by Joe Biden, had for months been reticent about approving the plaintiffs’ requests for work stoppages. The plaintiffs had argued the administration was moving ahead with work related to the project despite the pending lawsuit.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Her reluctance to issue orders ended in October, spurred in part by a tree-cutting spree by the administration over a holiday weekend with little notification to the judge or plaintiffs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Officials and government lawyers said the tree work was part of a 2019 plan that recommended the cutting. In response, the judge confronted the administration over what she portrayed as deceitful actions over its intentions for the project.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reyes has repeatedly expressed frustration over the minute planning details she has been asked to adjudicate, including over the trees being cut down at the 106-year-old park.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;The Associated Press contributed to this report&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/trump-golf-split.png?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/png\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">905d088b-2127-5c90-bfd2-c0550db72659</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/golf</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/us/washington-dc</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/person/donald-trump</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/politics/elections/local</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:00:05 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/dabo-swinney-reacts-clemson-hits-latest-low-upset-loss-georgia-tech-nobody-coming-save-us</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/dabo-swinney-reacts-clemson-hits-latest-low-upset-loss-georgia-tech-nobody-coming-save-us</guid> <title>Dabo Swinney reacts after Clemson hits latest low with upset loss to Georgia Tech: &apos;Nobody coming to save us&apos;</title>  <description>Georgia Tech rushed for 269 yards and handed Dabo Swinney one of his worst career losses as Clemson fell 20-6 at home to a team with a losing record.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;Georgia Tech coach Brent Key overhauled his staff this week, firing multiple assistants amid a four-game losing streak. The shake-up came as a season that began with high expectations spiraled into disappointment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/sports/ncaa/georgia-tech-yellow-jackets&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Yellow Jackets&lt;/a&gt; responded Saturday, ending their losing streak with an upset road win over Clemson. The Dabo Swinney coached Tigers managed just 228 total yards in the 20-6 defeat at Memorial Stadium.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The loss further dimmed Clemson’s &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/college-football-sells-another-piece-soul-cfp-officially-expanding-24-teams&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;ACC Championship game&lt;/a&gt; hopes and left the Tigers with injuries to both quarterbacks. Starter Tait Reynolds was forced to head to the locker room early with a leg injury, and Christopher Vizzina threw for 133 yards and an interception in relief. Vizzina went to the hospital after the game with his own injury.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLICK HERE FOR MORE OUTKICK SPORTS COVERAGE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Swinney reacted to the latest low point in Clemson’s season, acknowledging that any turnaround would have to come from within. &quot;It&apos;s difficult, but ain&apos;t nobody coming to save us, nobody cares, we&apos;ve got to find a way to get it done,&quot; Swinney said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/sports/ncaa/clemson-tigers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Clemson has now&lt;/a&gt; lost nine of its last 11 home games against Power Four opponents. Under Swinney, the Tigers once put together school-record 40 consecutive home games at Memorial Stadium from 2016 through 2022.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;It&apos;s frustrating; we&apos;ve not played well (at home) coming off two really good wins,&quot; Swinney continued. &quot;Really expected us to play great today. Great week of practice, but again, it didn&apos;t go our way. It&apos;s frustrating, but we don&apos;t make any excuses. We&apos;re not blaming it on injuries. We didn&apos;t get it done. It&apos;s my job.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/indiana-hoosiers-boost-college-football-playoff-hopes-27-13-win-usc-trojans&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;INDIANA HOOSIERS BOOST COLLEGE FOOTBALL PLAYOFF HOPES WITH 27-13 WIN OVER USC TROJANS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/ranking-power-4-college-football-head-coaching-job-most-likely-come-open-next&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RANKING WHICH POWER 4 COLLEGE FOOTBALL HEAD COACHING JOB IS MOST LIKELY TO COME OPEN NEXT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Georgia Tech rushed for 269 yards and two touchdowns. Swinney acknowledged how difficult it is to win when his defense struggles to contain the opposing team&apos;s run game.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;When you can&apos;t stop the run, you don&apos;t deserve to win,&quot; Swinney said. &quot;But you got to score enough points. We&apos;re not doing enough on offense. You don&apos;t win the line of scrimmage, you don&apos;t deserve to win; they did, give them credit.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Swinney’s 7-6 finish in 2025, his worst since 2010, raised questions about his future with the program. A season-opening blowout loss at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/sports/ncaa/lsu-tigers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;LSU&lt;/a&gt; further intensified scrutiny of his future and renewed attention on the $57 million buyout he would receive if fired this season.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Swinney is owed $60 million beginning in 2027, but a declining buyout schedule would lower Clemson’s obligation to $57 million if he is fired this fall. His contract does not include a mitigation clause, meaning if he lands another coaching job, Clemson would not get a discount on the amount the school owes him.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Clemson closes out its ACC regular-season schedule next Friday against Duke. Georgia Tech hosts Wake Forest next week in Atlanta.&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/dabo-swinney-clemson-georgia-tech.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">4b8d78f9-5e07-511c-95af-a76910660597</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa-fb</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa/georgia-tech-yellow-jackets</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa/clemson-tigers</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/betting</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:35:20 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/unc-asheville-player-makes-costly-mistake-after-miracle-3-pointer-could-have-forced-overtime</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/unc-asheville-player-makes-costly-mistake-after-miracle-3-pointer-could-have-forced-overtime</guid> <title>UNC Asheville player makes costly mistake after miracle 3-pointer that could have forced overtime</title>  <description>Myles Mayfield&amp;apos;s costly intentional foul after a game-tying 3-pointer gave Georgia Tech a stunning 75-74 win over UNC Asheville in the final seconds.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;At least one &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/sports/ncaa-bk&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;college basketball team&lt;/a&gt; is apparently knocking off the rust in the early going of the season.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;UNC Asheville lost a heartbreaker to &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/sports/ncaa/georgia-tech-yellow-jackets&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Georgia Tech&lt;/a&gt;, 75-74, just seconds after jubilation ensued due to a costly mistake.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Georgia Tech built a 74-71 advantage in the final seconds before Connor Dubsky hit a 3-pointer with 2.2 seconds remaining to tie it and likely send the game to overtime.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLICK HERE FOR MORE OUTKICK SPORTS COVERAGE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;However, apparently, UNC Asheville forward Myles Mayfield did not know what the score was, because he intentionally fouled a Yellow Jacket almost immediately.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Head coach &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/sports/ncaa&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Mike Morrell&lt;/a&gt; was in disbelief initially, but he and other players consoled Mayfield.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;That sent Victor Valdes to the free throw line, and he hit one of two to take the lead, and UNC Asheville was unable to get another shot off.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;UNC Asheville was up by 10 with 6:30 to go, so there is plenty of blame to go around. The Yellow Jackets (4-0) trailed 32-25 at halftime and were down by as many as 11 in the second half before rallying.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/top-ranked-georgia-rolls-past-missouri-moves-closer-sec-championship-game-return&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TOP-RANKED GEORGIA ROLLS PAST MISSOURI, MOVES CLOSER TO SEC CHAMPIONSHIP GAME RETURN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;To make matters worse, though, the mistake erased quite an effort from Mayfield, who scored 21 points on 9-of-11 shooting.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Georgia Tech overcame 37% shooting by grabbing 19 offensive rebounds and holding a 45-37 advantage on the glass.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Tylis Jordan added seven rebounds for Georgia Tech, while Jackson Fields finished with 14 points and 14 rebounds. Kam Craft scored 13 points and made four 3-pointers, and Kaiden Bailey added 11 off the bench.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;The Associated Press contributed to this report.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/myles-mayfield-unc-asheville-georgia-tech.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">a8a82897-af65-52ed-b7c5-2ee3be4a9f4d</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa-bk</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa/georgia-tech-yellow-jackets</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/betting</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:08:48 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/top-ranked-georgia-rolls-past-missouri-moves-closer-sec-championship-game-return</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/top-ranked-georgia-rolls-past-missouri-moves-closer-sec-championship-game-return</guid> <title>Top-ranked Georgia rolls past Missouri, moves closer to SEC championship game return</title>  <description>Nate Frazier&amp;apos;s three rushing touchdowns helped Georgia race to a 31-point halftime lead over Missouri in a dominant return to the No. 1 ranking.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;Georgia made the most of its return to No. 1. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/sports/ncaa/georgia-bulldogs&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;The Bulldogs&lt;/a&gt; jumped out to a 31-point first-half lead and went on to roll past Missouri 48-21 between the famed hedges at Sanford Stadium.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Georgia running back Nate Frazier rushed for three touchdowns, while quarterback Gunnar Stockton accounted for two more scores.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The performance marked a sharp turnaround from last month, when the Bulldogs first reached No. 1 before suffering a stunning home loss to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/unranked-auburn-stuns-top-ranked-georgia-walk-off-field-goal-feat-not-seen-36-years&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;the unranked Auburn Tigers.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLICK HERE FOR MORE OUTKICK SPORTS COVERAGE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Bulldogs avoided a repeat against another group of Tigers, scoring on their first five possessions. Frazier rushed for 72 yards. Stockton finished with 252 passing yards. Georgia held Missouri to 286 total yards, with much of the Tigers’ production coming after the outcome was decided.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The tone was set almost instantly when Raylen Wilson intercepted Austin Simmons on the first play from scrimmage. Wilson returned his first career pick 30 yards to the Missouri 7-yard line. Two plays later, Frazier scored on a 4-yard run, putting the Bulldogs ahead just 61 seconds into the game.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/kirby-smart-entered-dangerous-era-georgia-aggressive-win-alabama&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KIRBY SMART HAS ENTERED HIS MOST DANGEROUS ERA AFTER GEORGIA’S AGGRESSIVE WIN OVER ALABAMA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It only got worse for Mizzou.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stockton scored on an 8-yard touchdown run, Frazier capped an 87-yard drive with a 3-yard TD, Peyton Woodring booted a 41-yard field goal and Stockton capped the barrage with a 12-yard scoring pass to Isiah Canion just past the midway point of the second quarter.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Simmons threw for 175 yards and three touchdowns, but most of his production only made the final score a bit more respectable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Georgia has cruised to victory in each of their last three games — &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/good-luck-sec-auburn-awoke-monster-athens-florida-pays-price-georgia-cocktail-beatdown&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;dominating Florida&lt;/a&gt;, Ole Miss and now Mizzou by a combined score of 117-36.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Georgia travels to South Carolina next week to close out its SEC regular-season schedule. Missouri hosts Kentucky.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;The Associated Press contributed to this report.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/Georgia-Missouri.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">14829c9b-8c9b-53ed-bb86-27c71308df96</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa-fb</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa/georgia-bulldogs</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa/missouri-tigers</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/betting</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:30:05 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/entertainment/kristin-cavallari-steamy-bedroom-confession-ahead-40th-birthday</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/entertainment/kristin-cavallari-steamy-bedroom-confession-ahead-40th-birthday</guid> <title>Kristin Cavallari makes steamy bedroom confession ahead of 40th birthday</title>  <description>Kristin Cavallari revealed intimate details about her sex life on her &amp;quot;Let&amp;apos;s Be Honest&amp;quot; podcast as she looks ahead to her upcoming 40th birthday.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/person/kristin-cavallari&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Kristin Cavallari&lt;/a&gt; is giving fans an inside look at what goes on in her bedroom in a steamy confession on her podcast.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In a recent episode of her &quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FXk5fKV-ww8&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;Let&apos;s Be Honest&lt;/a&gt;&quot; podcast, the 39-year-old reality star opened up about her upcoming 40th birthday and gave some insight into her sex life, noting she isn&apos;t having sex but says: &quot;Your sex drive as you get older is like wild.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Like age 40, I&apos;m way more sexual than I was at 25. Again, it would be nice if I had an outlet for it, but we can have sex with ourselves, which is what I f---ing do all the time,&quot; she said. &quot;But that&apos;s one of the reasons why I can&apos;t wait to be in a relationship is I feel like I&apos;ve become this like sexual being.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;She explained that her last relationship &quot;was a very sexual relationship,&quot; but that that was something she needed, and admits it is something she misses.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/entertainment/kristin-cavallari-flaunts-her-toned-figure-bikinis-during-european-summer-vacation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KRISTIN CAVALLARI FLAUNTS HER TONED FIGURE IN BIKINIS DURING EUROPEAN SUMMER VACATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cavallari added that she is now looking forward to turning 40, saying, &quot;If this is what 40s is, like f- - - yeah. This is fun.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Earlier in the episode, the &quot;Very Cavallari&quot; star quipped that it &quot;takes one to two years of abstinence to become a nun&quot; and that she is on her way towards that achievement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The reality star was previously married to former professional football quarterback &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/kristin-cavallari-doubles-down-controversial-claim-divorce-jay-cutler&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Jay Cutler&lt;/a&gt; from 2013 to 2020, when she announced they were getting a divorce. They share three children; Camden, 14, Jaxon, 12, and Saylor, 10.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;When speaking about her divorce, on the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WWPU1fx6u44&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;&quot;Aspire with Emma Grede&quot;&lt;/a&gt; podcast in July 2026, the &quot;Laguna Beach&quot; star claimed she gained the confidence to leave her marriage because of the success of her company, Uncommon James.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/newsletters?cmpid=fnfirstnl&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GET ENTERTAINMENT SCOOP DELIVERED RIGHT TO YOUR EMAIL BY CLICKING HERE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Which is interesting because if I didn&apos;t have Uncommon James, I could have taken half of his money, right? But because I had this company, there was a really large asset on our balance sheet,&quot; she said. &quot;I didn&apos;t get anything, which I&apos;m so happy about now. But I don&apos;t get any money from my ex-husband. I had to give him half the value of Uncommon James in cash and properties and everything else. Yeah. Isn&apos;t that interesting?&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Following her divorce, she dated Mark Estes for a few months in 2024 and country singer &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-culture/morgan-wallen-more-music-way-winds-down-im-problem-era-career&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Morgan Wallen&lt;/a&gt;. She told Bunnie XO on the &quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/kristin-cavallari-evolution-of-me/id1465273008?i=1000682121758&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;Dumb Blonde&lt;/a&gt;&quot; podcast in December 2024 that Wallen &quot;was good in bed.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;I&apos;ll be honest with you. He was the first guy in my f---ing life that wasn’t just completely enamored with me ... It really threw me,&quot; she said. &quot;I love having the upper hand and I feel like with him, I didn&apos;t have the upper hand.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/entertainment&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LIKE WHAT YOU&apos;RE READING? CLICK HERE FOR MORE ENTERTAINMENT NEWS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;She later shared in an April 2025 episode of her podcast that she was in a relationship with former NHL player Nate Thompson but that they had called things off in March.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/entertainment/entertainment-quizzes&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PUT YOUR ENTERTAINMENT KNOWLEDGE TO THE TEST AND SEE HOW YOU SCORE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;She shared that while he was &quot;the most honest, pure, amazing, quote-unquote relationship,&quot; she had experienced, she decided to call it quits after realizing she &quot;just didn&apos;t wanna be in a relationship.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;He is an ex-hockey player. He&apos;s been retired for a couple years now. He&apos;s a dad. He&apos;s someone who has done a lot of work on himself, and we really connected on such a deep level,&quot; she explained. &quot;Honestly, one of the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/entertainment/events/couples#&amp;amp;_intcmp=fnc_search-results_search_main-content_search-topics_3_1_celebrity-couples&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;deeper relationships I&apos;ve had&lt;/a&gt;, especially in such a short amount of time.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/524/kristin-cavallari-new-york-june-2025.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"524\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">3c905a79-f32c-5a19-aaa4-0a8dc438c217</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/person/kristin-cavallari</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/entertainment</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/entertainment/events/couples</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/entertainment/genres/reality</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/entertainment/tv</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/entertainment</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:00:51 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/indiana-hoosiers-boost-college-football-playoff-hopes-27-13-win-usc-trojans</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/indiana-hoosiers-boost-college-football-playoff-hopes-27-13-win-usc-trojans</guid> <title>Indiana Hoosiers boost College Football Playoff hopes with 27-13 win over USC Trojans</title>  <description>Indiana&amp;apos;s defense forced costly USC Trojans turnovers in the red zone as the Hoosiers moved to 9-1 and kept their playoff hopes firmly alive.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/sports/ncaa/indiana-hoosiers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Indiana Hoosiers&apos;&lt;/a&gt; hopes of making the College Football Playoff and defending their national title are still alive thanks to a 27-13 win over the USC Trojans.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It&apos;s kind of hard to believe that &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/sports/ncaa/usc-trojans&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;USC&lt;/a&gt; and Indiana had only played five times going into Saturday&apos;s game in Bloomington, and boy, was this one big.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Both teams came in facing what was effectively a &quot;must-win&quot; scenario as far as having a shot at the College Football Playoff.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/cfp-reaction-alabama-feels-love-indiana-gets-shaft-big-12-gets-relief-committee-confuses-us&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CFP REACTION: ALABAMA FEELS THE LOVE, INDIANA GETS THE SHAFT AND BIG 12 GETS RELIEF AS COMMITTEE CONFUSES US&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lincoln Riley and the Trojans have struggled on the road, and that&apos;s what they were facing on Saturday. As for the Hoosiers, their ground game took a hit before the game even began when running back Turbo Richard was ruled out.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Both defenses were clicking in the first half, which put points at a premium. Indiana struck first when QB Grant Wilson hit tight end Brock Schott for six.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Somewhat strangely, both teams missed field goals in the first half, but each of them made up for it with another. That made it a 10-7 game with under a minute until halftime.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;That&apos;s when USC&apos;s Deven Bryant picked off Wilson, putting the ball back in quarterback Jayden Maiava&apos;s hands.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;After a 51-yard bomb to Kayden Dixon-Wyatt, Maiava hit wideout Zacharyus Williams for a 7-yard touchdown to tie it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLICK HERE FOR MORE OUTKICK SPORTS COVERAGE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Each team added a field goal early in the second half, and then Indiana pulled ahead thanks to a five-play, 75-yard drive, capped off by a Khobie Martin touchdown.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;USC followed with a lengthy drive that ended early in the fourth quarter with a field goal attempt to cut the Indiana lead to four.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;However, kicker Caden Chittenden — who came in after Ryon Sayeri missed a field goal on the first drive of the game — missed a kick of his own, costing the Trojans some much-needed points.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Later in the quarter, the Trojans found themselves deep in Hoosier territory, but once again, they left points on the board when Maiava threw an interception in the red zone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It proved to be even costlier than that, as the Hoosiers took the ball 93 yards, most of it thanks to a 42-yard touchdown pass to Charlie Becker.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Those miscues for USC added up, and the final one came on 4th-and-13 at their own end of the field. Maiava — who, in fairness, was running out of options to keep his team in it — threw a prayer downfield, only for it to be picked off by defensive back Jamari Sharpe.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;That was all she wrote. A third loss on the year means it&apos;s pretty much curtains for &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/college-football-playoff-rankings-georgia-rises-no-1-notre-dame-cracks-top-5-big-win-miami&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;USC&apos;s playoff hopes&lt;/a&gt;, while Indiana moves to 9-1 on the year and 6-1 in Big Ten play.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Hoosiers will head out to Washington next week to take on the Huskies, while USC will look to bounce back against the struggling &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/outkick-sports/not-even-chance-free-tuition-could-get-maryland-students-seats-football-saturday&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Maryland Terrapins&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/indiana-usc-2.png?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/png\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">75e347a8-622a-58fb-9c96-770a64db60fa</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa-fb</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa/indiana-hoosiers</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/sports/ncaa/usc-trojans</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/outkick/betting</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/outkick-sports</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:00:18 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/world/robot-dogs-mounted-rifles-deployed-anti-gang-stadium-operation-haiti</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/world/robot-dogs-mounted-rifles-deployed-anti-gang-stadium-operation-haiti</guid> <title>Robot dogs mounted with rifles deployed in anti-gang stadium operation in Haiti</title>  <description>El Salvador President Nayib Bukele shared video of armed robot dogs storming Sylvio Cator Stadium as forces joined Haitian police in a gang crackdown on the violent island nation.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;El Salvador President Nayib Bukele released a video this week showing military forces using &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/category/tech/topics/military-tech&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;robotic dogs&lt;/a&gt; mounted with rifles in an operation to take back a stadium in Haiti from gang control.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Under the bilateral agreement between the Haitian government and the government of &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/travel/regions/central-america&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;El Salvador&lt;/a&gt;, a joint operation involving the Haitian National Police, the Haitian Armed Forces (FAd’H), the Task Force, and the Salvadoran Special Forces successfully took control of Sylvio Cator Stadium and secured it,&quot; Bukele wrote on X in a translation from Haitian Creole.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The video showed the robots moving down a hallway and up a set of stairs with the rifle on top.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/world/el-salvador-air-assault-destroys-haiti-gang-headquarters-search-missing-troops&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EL SALVADOR-BACKED AIR ASSAULT DESTROYS HAITI GANG HEADQUARTERS AMID SEARCH FOR MISSING TROOPS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It’s unclear exactly how the robots assisted in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/world/world-regions/caribbean-region&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Port-au-Prince&lt;/a&gt; operation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bukele said &quot;several human skulls&quot; were found inside the stadium during the operation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/politics/they-fed-him-his-own-ears-top-republican-shares-horrifying-stories-gang-rule-haiti&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&apos;THEY FED HIM HIS OWN EARS&apos;: TOP REPUBLICAN SHARES HORRIFYING STORIES OF GANG RULE IN HAITI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;We will now establish an operational base at the stadium so we can continue advancing deeper into territory controlled by the gangs,&quot; he said. &quot;We now have the upper hand on the ground.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bukele demanded gang members leave the area before their offensive began.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/opinion/john-koufos-trumps-shield-americas-could-help-defend-us-from-cartels&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JOHN KOUFOS: TRUMP’S ‘SHIELD OF THE AMERICAS’ COULD HELP DEFEND US FROM CARTELS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Those who choose to stay and fight our forces will have to face the consequences,&quot; he said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cracking down &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/world/bukeles-warning-haitian-gang-leaders-forces-finish-el-salvador&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;on gangs&lt;/a&gt; has been a hallmark of Bukele’s presidency since he took office in 2019.&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/robot-el-salvdor.gif\" type=\"image/gif\" expression=\"full\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">38cace3c-fdd8-5a56-8126-8adbbac664c5</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/tech/technologies/robots</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/world/world-regions/caribbean-region</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/travel/regions/central-america</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/fox-nation/caught-on-camera</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/tech/topics/military-tech</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/world</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/world</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:51:47 -0500</pubDate> </item>      <item> <link>https://www.foxnews.com/health/millions-americans-use-marijuana-sleep-study-raises-troubling-questions</link> <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://www.foxnews.com/health/millions-americans-use-marijuana-sleep-study-raises-troubling-questions</guid> <title>Millions of Americans use marijuana to sleep, but new study raises troubling questions</title>  <description>A Northwestern Medicine study found that marijuana users had objectively worse sleep quality, even though they didn&amp;apos;t perceive their sleep as worse. Other experts weighed in.</description>  <content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;Marijuana may be making sleep quality worse, despite its widespread use as a sleep aid, a recent Northwestern Medicine study found.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The findings of &lt;a href=&quot;https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jamanetworkopen/fullarticle/2855118?utm_campaign=articlePDF&amp;amp;utm_medium=articlePDFlink&amp;amp;utm_source=articlePDF&amp;amp;utm_content=jamanetworkopen.2026.38303&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;the study&lt;/a&gt;, which included 1,266 participants, showed that both lifetime and recent cannabis users objectively had worse sleep quality, although they did not report their sleep to be worse.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Participants were monitored for almost 35 years, from young adulthood into middle age, with scientists tracking their use of cannabis over time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/health/america-hits-major-marijuana-milestone-daily-weed-use-surpasses-daily-drinking&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AMERICA HITS MAJOR MARIJUANA MILESTONE AS DAILY WEED USE SURPASSES DAILY DRINKING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In middle age, participants wore a sleep monitor on their wrist for a week and filled out surveys about their &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/health/sleep-disorders&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;sleep quality&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This allowed researchers to compare objective and subjective reports of participants’ sleep.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Our data do not support the belief that cannabis is helpful as a sleep aid,&quot; said senior study author Mercedes R. Carnethon, Ph.D., as Northwestern Now reported.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;As &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/health/cannabis&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;cannabis becomes&lt;/a&gt; increasingly available and accepted, it&apos;s important to better understand its long-term associations with health behaviors such as sleep,&quot; Carnethon added.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/newsletters?cmpid=fnfirstnl&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLICK HERE TO SIGN UP FOR OUR LIFESTYLE NEWSLETTER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Among all participants, a greater lifetime exposure to marijuana was linked to worse objective sleep quality.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Those who had a higher cannabis usage over time were generally asleep for a lower percentage of the night and experienced more &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/health/trouble-sleeping-neighborhood-partly-blame-experts-say&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;sleep disruption&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Similarly, recent cannabis users were more likely to have more sleep fragmentation and lower sleep efficiency, compared to people who never used the substance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The study also found there was a much higher chance that recent &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/health/marijuana-use-rises-sharply-among-one-group-americans-new-study-finds&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;cannabis users&lt;/a&gt; would sleep longer than eight hours per night. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The study discusses the differences between objective and subjective reports of sleep quality.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/lifestyle&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLICK HERE FOR MORE LIFESTYLE NEWS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;What makes this study particularly interesting is that participants who used cannabis demonstrated objectively poorer sleep, yet their own assessments of sleep quality did not reflect those differences,&quot; Alfred Joshua, M.D., a board-certified emergency medicine physician based in California, told Fox News Digital. (He was not involved with the new study.)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;In other words, someone may believe marijuana is helping them sleep, while objective measurements suggest otherwise.&quot; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Researchers considered multiple outside factors including age, race, sex, smoking frequency, alcohol consumption, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/health/nutrition-and-fitness/fitness&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;physical activity&lt;/a&gt; and more.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Even with these factors taken into account, the study found a consistent correlation between &lt;a href=&quot;https://foxnews.com/health/men-women-smoke-marijuana-may-experience-different-effects-study-suggests&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;cannabis use&lt;/a&gt; and poorer objectively measured sleep.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The mode of cannabis consumption, such as smoking versus taking edibles, was not considered.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;It is not surprising that the actual quality of sleep of these subjects, after chronic marijuana use, is poor compared to those who do not smoke marijuana because people who claim that they need to smoke marijuana before they go to sleep, in order to relax, are only kidding themselves,&quot; board-certified psychiatrist Carole Lieberman, M.D., of California told Fox News Digital. (She, too, was not affiliated with the new study.)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;It is more a psychological addiction than a physical one,&quot; she added. &quot;They enjoy the high that they get right away, but the marijuana doesn&apos;t help them to sleep better.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/lifestyle/quizzes&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TEST YOURSELF WITH OUR LATEST LIFESTYLE QUIZ&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;The researchers found that greater cumulative cannabis exposure was associated with reduced sleep efficiency, increased sleep fragmentation and more time spent awake after initially falling asleep,&quot; said Joshua, the board-certified emergency medicine physician. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;These findings raise important questions about whether habitual marijuana use is a sustainable strategy for managing sleep problems,&quot; he added. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fox News Digital recently reported on other cannabis findings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A study of nearly 450,000 American adults, for instance, linked &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/health/marijuana-users-may-face-hidden-driving-danger-standard-tests-miss&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;cannabis use&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; to an increased risk of stroke and cardiovascular disease.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The findings were scheduled for presentation at the American Heart Association’s Scientific Sessions 2026 in Chicago Nov. 6–9. They showed that both casual and heavy marijuana users have higher odds of &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foxnews.com/category/health/heart-health&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;heart conditions&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; compared to non-users.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;Khloe Quill of Fox News Digital contributed reporting. &lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>    <media:content url=\"https://a57.foxnews.com/static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/11/931/523/couple-relaxing-smoking-marijuana-joint.jpg?ve=1&amp;tl=1\" type=\"image/jpeg\" expression=\"full\" width=\"931\" height=\"523\" />     <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.identifier\">1ebae5ff-6e51-50cd-bcd2-94de25ee8602</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/prism.channel\">fnc</category> <category domain=\"foxnews.com/metadata/dc.source\">Fox News</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/health</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/health/cannabis</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/health/sleep-disorders</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/lifestyle</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/health/wellness</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/health/mental-health/drug-and-substance-abuse</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/taxonomy\">fox-news/health/mental-health</category>   <category domain=\"foxnews.com/section-path\">fox-news/health</category>  <category domain=\"foxnews.com/content-type\">article</category> <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:45:30 -0500</pubDate> </item>                        </channel></rss>","fetchedAt":"2026-11-15T12:59:07.864Z"},"nbc":{"xml":"<rss xmlns:media=\"http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xmlns:dcterms=\"http://purl.org/dc/terms/\" xmlns:content=\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\" version=\"2.0\"><channel><title>NBC News Top Stories</title><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/</link><description>NBC News Top Stories</description><language>en-US</language><copyright>© 2026 NBCNews.com</copyright><lastBuildDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:46:52 GMT</lastBuildDate><image><url>https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/MSNBC/Components/Media/NBC-promo-graphics/nbc-news.png</url><title>NBC News Top Stories</title><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/</link></image><item><dc:creator>Gary Grumbach</dc:creator><dc:creator>Raquel Coronell Uribe</dc:creator><dc:creator>Michael Kosnar</dc:creator><dc:creator>Dareh Gregorian</dc:creator><dateTimeWritten>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:46:52 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>The Trump administration cannot close East Potomac Park to the public for now, a federal judge in Washington ruled Saturday, dealing a blow to the president’s effort to renovate its golf course.</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/trump-administration/judge-temporarily-blocks-trumps-plan-redevelop-east-potomac-golf-cours-rcna609366</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/trump-administration/judge-temporarily-blocks-trumps-plan-redevelop-east-potomac-golf-cours-rcna609366</link><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-10/261019-potomac-golf-course-vl-1048a-48c250.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1333\" width=\"2000\"><media:credit>Mark Schiefelbein</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">A golfer walks past the stump of a large tree outside on the golf course while carrying a bag of golf clubs</media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">The judge&#39;s order does not require the administration to continue operating the golf course.</media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-10/261019-potomac-golf-course-vl-1048a-48c250.jpg\" height=\"1333\" width=\"2000\"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:46:52 GMT</pubDate><title>Judge temporarily halts Trump’s ‘Trash Island’ golf course redevelopment in D.C.</title><updateDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:46:52 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>Dennis Romero</dc:creator><dateTimeWritten>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:14:35 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>Former “Saturday Night Live” repertory player and writer Bowen Yang returned to help open the show this weekend with his portrayal of former Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang.</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/pop-culture/pop-culture-news/bowen-yang-returns-snl-ex-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-mary-todd-lincoln-rcna609381</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/pop-culture/pop-culture-news/bowen-yang-returns-snl-ex-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-mary-todd-lincoln-rcna609381</link><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261115-snl-cold-open-cc-1223a-5c8e72.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1080\" width=\"1920\"><media:credit>NBC</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">Image: Former &#34;Saturday Night Live&#34; cast member Bowen Yang made a surprise appearance at the show&#39;s cold open Nov. 14, 2026.</media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">Former &#34;Saturday Night Live&#34; cast member Bowen Yang made a surprise appearance at the show&#39;s cold open, playing former Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang. </media:description></media:content><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261115-snl-yang-lincoln-cc-0209a-f7ae6d.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1080\" width=\"1920\"><media:credit>NBC</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">Image: Bowen Yang as Mary Todd Lincoln in the Lincoln Tunnel on &#34;Saturday Night Live,&#34; on Nov. 15, 2026. </media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">Former &#34;Saturday Night Live&#34; cast member Bowen Yang made a surprise appearance at the show&#39;s cold open, playing former Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang. </media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261115-snl-cold-open-cc-1223a-5c8e72.jpg\" height=\"1080\" width=\"1920\"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:14:35 GMT</pubDate><title>Bowen Yang returns to ‘SNL’ to spoof Jensen Huang amid Nvidia spy scandal</title><updateDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:25:38 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>Isabella O&#39;Connor</dc:creator><dateTimeWritten>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>Women with autoimmune diseases such as lupus or rheumatoid arthritis are more likely to be misdiagnosed or get delayed treatment compared with men, with their symptoms often dismissed as “psychological.”</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/health/womens-health/autoimmune-diseases-women-lupus-arthritis-misdiagnosed-study-rcna609176</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/health/womens-health/autoimmune-diseases-women-lupus-arthritis-misdiagnosed-study-rcna609176</link><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261113-arthritis-sjr-1148-4870ce.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1709\" width=\"2500\"><media:credit>BSIP</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">Rheumatoid Arthritis, X-Ray</media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">Women with autoimmune diseases such as lupus or rheumatoid arthritis are more likely to be misdiagnosed or get delayed treatment compared to men.</media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261113-arthritis-sjr-1148-4870ce.jpg\" height=\"1709\" width=\"2500\"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><title>Women with autoimmune diseases often misdiagnosed for 4 years or more</title><updateDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>Ben Kamisar</dc:creator><dateTimeWritten>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:52:49 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>Former Democratic Rep. Mary Peltola is likely to win Alaska’s Senate race, according to an NBC News Decision Desk analysis, as vote-counting continues in the state.</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/democrat-mary-peltola-likely-win-alaska-senate-race-rcna608673</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/democrat-mary-peltola-likely-win-alaska-senate-race-rcna608673</link><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261110-Mary-Peltola-vsb-2055-bf3719.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1801\" width=\"2500\"><media:credit>Justin Sullivan</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">Mary Peltola.</media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">Former Democratic Rep. Mary Peltola speaks during an election night watch party in Anchorage, Alaska.</media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261110-Mary-Peltola-vsb-2055-bf3719.jpg\" height=\"1801\" width=\"2500\"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:52:49 GMT</pubDate><title>Democrat Mary Peltola is likely to win Alaska’s Senate race, as vote counting continues</title><updateDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:52:49 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>Erik Ortiz</dc:creator><dateTimeWritten>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 12:00:39 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>If you’re a student borrower who was required to transition to another plan this year, share your story.</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/news/education/changes-student-loan-repayment-plans-share-experience-rcna607624</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/news/education/changes-student-loan-repayment-plans-share-experience-rcna607624</link><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261105-graduation-vl-101p-197d18.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1333\" width=\"2000\"><media:credit>Edwin Tan</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">Convocation ceremony rear view Graduation university students together with Dean standing on stage for photograph session in a row</media:text><media:description type=\"plain\"></media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261105-graduation-vl-101p-197d18.jpg\" height=\"1333\" width=\"2000\"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 12:00:39 GMT</pubDate><title>We want to hear your experience with changes to student loan repayment plans</title><updateDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 12:00:39 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dateTimeWritten>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 16:05:35 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>A magnificent Norway spruce has made its journey from West Edmeston, New York, to Rockefeller Center. The tree will undergo a glow-up ahead of the lighting ceremony on Dec. 2.</description><expires>2056-11-07T16:04:53.000+0000</expires><guid isPermaLink=\"false\">tdy_sat_tree_arrival_261107</guid><link>https://www.today.com/video/2026-rockefeller-center-christmas-tree-arrives-in-new-york-city-273069125683</link><media:content url=\"https://prodamdnewsencoding.akamaized.net/NBC_News_Digital/tdy_sat_tree_arrival_261107/1/abs/index.m3u8\" medium=\"video\"><media:credit></media:credit><media:title>2026 Rockefeller Center Christmas Tree Arrives in New York City</media:title><media:player url=\"https://www.today.com/video/2026-rockefeller-center-christmas-tree-arrives-in-new-york-city-273069125683\"></media:player><media:thumbnail url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/mpx/2704722219/2026_11/1794067481071_tdy_sat_tree_arrival_261107_S3_1920x1080-v679qn.jpg\"></media:thumbnail><media:description type=\"plain\">A magnificent Norway spruce has made its journey from West Edmeston, New York, to Rockefeller Center. The tree will undergo a glow-up ahead of the lighting ceremony on Dec. 2.</media:description><media:subTitle type=\"text/srt\" lang=\"en-US\" url=\"https://prodamdnewsencoding.akamaized.net/NBC_News_Digital/nbcnews/captions/2026/11/1794067481071_tdy_sat_tree_arrival_261107.srt\"></media:subTitle><media:subTitle type=\"text/vtt\" lang=\"en-US\" url=\"https://prodamdnewsencoding.akamaized.net/NBC_News_Digital/nbcnews/captions/2026/11/1794067481071_tdy_sat_tree_arrival_261107.vtt\"></media:subTitle></media:content><media:thumbnail url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/mpx/2704722219/2026_11/1794067481071_tdy_sat_tree_arrival_261107_S3_1920x1080-v679qn.jpg\"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 16:04:48 GMT</pubDate><title>2026 Rockefeller Center Christmas Tree Arrives in New York City</title><updateDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 16:05:35 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>Isabella O&#39;Connor</dc:creator><dateTimeWritten>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>Women with autoimmune diseases such as lupus or rheumatoid arthritis are more likely to be misdiagnosed or get delayed treatment compared with men, with their symptoms often dismissed as “psychological.”</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/health/womens-health/autoimmune-diseases-women-lupus-arthritis-misdiagnosed-study-rcna609176</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/health/womens-health/autoimmune-diseases-women-lupus-arthritis-misdiagnosed-study-rcna609176</link><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261113-arthritis-sjr-1148-4870ce.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1709\" width=\"2500\"><media:credit>BSIP</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">Rheumatoid Arthritis, X-Ray</media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">Women with autoimmune diseases such as lupus or rheumatoid arthritis are more likely to be misdiagnosed or get delayed treatment compared to men.</media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261113-arthritis-sjr-1148-4870ce.jpg\" height=\"1709\" width=\"2500\"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><title>Women with autoimmune diseases often misdiagnosed for 4 years or more</title><updateDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>The Associated Press</dc:creator><dateTimeWritten>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:04:56 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>MANILA, Philippines — Southeast Asian leaders opened their annual summit in the Philippine capital Manila on Sunday for three days of talks, including dialogues with world leaders led by U.S.</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/world/asia/southeast-asian-leaders-annual-summit-major-conflicts-impact-rcna609385</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/world/asia/southeast-asian-leaders-annual-summit-major-conflicts-impact-rcna609385</link><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261115-manila-nd-349b81.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"3488\" width=\"5232\"><media:credit>Eloisa Lopez </media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">Philippines Hosts ASEAN Summit And Related Meetings</media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">Philippine President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. hands the Digital Economy Framework Agreement (DECA) to ASEAN Secretary-General Kao Kim Hourn, while Philippine Secretary of Trade and Industry Maria Cristina Roque looks on .</media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261115-manila-nd-349b81.jpg\" height=\"3488\" width=\"5232\"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:04:56 GMT</pubDate><title>Southeast Asian leaders open annual summit with major conflicts topping the agenda</title><updateDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:04:56 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>Dennis Romero</dc:creator><dateTimeWritten>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:14:35 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>Former “Saturday Night Live” repertory player and writer Bowen Yang returned to help open the show this weekend with his portrayal of former Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang.</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/pop-culture/pop-culture-news/bowen-yang-returns-snl-ex-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-mary-todd-lincoln-rcna609381</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/pop-culture/pop-culture-news/bowen-yang-returns-snl-ex-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-mary-todd-lincoln-rcna609381</link><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261115-snl-cold-open-cc-1223a-5c8e72.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1080\" width=\"1920\"><media:credit>NBC</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">Image: Former &#34;Saturday Night Live&#34; cast member Bowen Yang made a surprise appearance at the show&#39;s cold open Nov. 14, 2026.</media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">Former &#34;Saturday Night Live&#34; cast member Bowen Yang made a surprise appearance at the show&#39;s cold open, playing former Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang. </media:description></media:content><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261115-snl-yang-lincoln-cc-0209a-f7ae6d.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1080\" width=\"1920\"><media:credit>NBC</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">Image: Bowen Yang as Mary Todd Lincoln in the Lincoln Tunnel on &#34;Saturday Night Live,&#34; on Nov. 15, 2026. </media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">Former &#34;Saturday Night Live&#34; cast member Bowen Yang made a surprise appearance at the show&#39;s cold open, playing former Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang. </media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261115-snl-cold-open-cc-1223a-5c8e72.jpg\" height=\"1080\" width=\"1920\"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:14:35 GMT</pubDate><title>Bowen Yang returns to ‘SNL’ to spoof Jensen Huang amid Nvidia spy scandal</title><updateDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:25:38 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>Gary Grumbach</dc:creator><dc:creator>Raquel Coronell Uribe</dc:creator><dc:creator>Michael Kosnar</dc:creator><dc:creator>Dareh Gregorian</dc:creator><dateTimeWritten>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:46:52 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>The Trump administration cannot close East Potomac Park to the public for now, a federal judge in Washington ruled Saturday, dealing a blow to the president’s effort to renovate its golf course.</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/trump-administration/judge-temporarily-blocks-trumps-plan-redevelop-east-potomac-golf-cours-rcna609366</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/trump-administration/judge-temporarily-blocks-trumps-plan-redevelop-east-potomac-golf-cours-rcna609366</link><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-10/261019-potomac-golf-course-vl-1048a-48c250.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1333\" width=\"2000\"><media:credit>Mark Schiefelbein</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">A golfer walks past the stump of a large tree outside on the golf course while carrying a bag of golf clubs</media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">The judge&#39;s order does not require the administration to continue operating the golf course.</media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-10/261019-potomac-golf-course-vl-1048a-48c250.jpg\" height=\"1333\" width=\"2000\"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:46:52 GMT</pubDate><title>Judge temporarily halts Trump’s ‘Trash Island’ golf course redevelopment in D.C.</title><updateDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:46:52 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>John Lapinski</dc:creator><dc:creator>Stephen Pettigrew</dc:creator><dc:creator>Marc Trussler</dc:creator><dateTimeWritten>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:22:15 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>As Alaska continues to count and report votes weeks after Election Day, it is increasingly unlikely that Republican Sen.</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/mary-peltola-track-win-alaska-even-ranked-choice-ballots-come-play-rcna609299</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/mary-peltola-track-win-alaska-even-ranked-choice-ballots-come-play-rcna609299</link><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261114-alaska-midterms-ch-0910-cb356d.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1666\" width=\"2500\"><media:credit>Christian Moorman</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">People cast their vote.</media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">Voters fill out ballots in Anchorage, Alaska, on Nov. 3.</media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261114-alaska-midterms-ch-0910-cb356d.jpg\" height=\"1666\" width=\"2500\"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:22:15 GMT</pubDate><title>Why Mary Peltola is on track to win in Alaska, even if ranked choice ballots come into play</title><updateDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:22:15 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>Doha Madani</dc:creator><dateTimeWritten>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:21:47 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>Costco members who love a whipped topping may consider going à la mode with their favorite dessert instead after the retailer’s Kirkland-brand whipped cream was recalled.</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/costco-brand-whipped-cream-recalled-rcna609344</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/costco-brand-whipped-cream-recalled-rcna609344</link><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261114-Cotco-aa-405-09550b.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1467\" width=\"2200\"><media:credit>Gary Hershorn</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">Costco Wholesale in Bayonne, New Jersey</media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">The whipped cream was sold in 12 states.</media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261114-Cotco-aa-405-09550b.jpg\" height=\"1467\" width=\"2200\"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:21:47 GMT</pubDate><title>Costco-brand whipped cream recalled over potential presence of cleaning chemical</title><updateDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:21:47 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>Ben Kamisar</dc:creator><dateTimeWritten>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:52:49 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>Former Democratic Rep. Mary Peltola is likely to win Alaska’s Senate race, according to an NBC News Decision Desk analysis, as vote-counting continues in the state.</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/democrat-mary-peltola-likely-win-alaska-senate-race-rcna608673</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/democrat-mary-peltola-likely-win-alaska-senate-race-rcna608673</link><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261110-Mary-Peltola-vsb-2055-bf3719.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1801\" width=\"2500\"><media:credit>Justin Sullivan</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">Mary Peltola.</media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">Former Democratic Rep. Mary Peltola speaks during an election night watch party in Anchorage, Alaska.</media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261110-Mary-Peltola-vsb-2055-bf3719.jpg\" height=\"1801\" width=\"2500\"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:52:49 GMT</pubDate><title>Democrat Mary Peltola is likely to win Alaska’s Senate race, as vote counting continues</title><updateDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:52:49 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>Andrew Greif</dc:creator><dateTimeWritten>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:04:00 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>Fernando Mendoza, the Heisman-winning quarterback selected No. 1 overall in last year’s NFL draft, takes over as starter for the Las Vegas Raiders. Will he turn around the franchise?</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/sports/nfl/fernando-mendoza-las-vegas-raiders-seattle-seahawks-kirk-cousins-rcna608889</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/sports/nfl/fernando-mendoza-las-vegas-raiders-seattle-seahawks-kirk-cousins-rcna608889</link><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261111-Fernando-Mendoza-bills-nfl-ww-1716-390bc7.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1667\" width=\"2500\"><media:credit>Cooper Neill</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">Fernando Mendoza getting ready to throw a football.</media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">Las Vegas Raiders quarterback Fernando Mendoza warms up prior to the team&#39;s game against the Buffalo Bills last month.</media:description></media:content><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261111-Fernando-Mendoza-heisman-ww-1716-30f966.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1666\" width=\"2500\"><media:credit>Adam Hunger</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">Fernando Mendoza grins while holding the Heisman Trophy.</media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">Las Vegas Raiders quarterback Fernando Mendoza warms up prior to the team&#39;s game against the Buffalo Bills last month.</media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261111-Fernando-Mendoza-bills-nfl-ww-1716-390bc7.jpg\" height=\"1667\" width=\"2500\"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:04:00 GMT</pubDate><title>He was drafted as an NFL team’s future. It arrives now.</title><updateDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:04:00 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>Rohan Nadkarni</dc:creator><dateTimeWritten>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:42:41 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>A Federal Aviation Administration ground stop that lasted more than four hours and canceled over 7,000 flights Friday affected the travel plans for several pro and college teams across multiple sports.</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/sports/college-football/faa-ground-stop-college-football-nfl-nba-nhl-rcna609309</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/sports/college-football/faa-ground-stop-college-football-nfl-nba-nhl-rcna609309</link><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261114-Oklahoma-Memorial-Stadium-ch-1110-0b9e72.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1667\" width=\"2500\"><media:credit>Brian Bahr</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">Oklahoma Memorial Stadium.</media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">Gaylord Family Oklahoma Memorial Stadium before a game between the Oklahoma Sooners and the New Mexico Lobos on Sept. 19, 2026 in Norman, Okla.</media:description></media:content><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261114-Duane-Heydt-ch-1129-01dc03.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1667\" width=\"2500\"><media:credit>Alika Jenner</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">Duane Heydt.</media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">NFL referee Duane Heydt in Seattle on Oct. 25.</media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261114-Oklahoma-Memorial-Stadium-ch-1110-0b9e72.jpg\" height=\"1667\" width=\"2500\"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:42:41 GMT</pubDate><title>FAA ground stop throws college football into chaos, while the NFL is safe</title><updateDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:42:41 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>Bethany Heitman</dc:creator><dateTimeWritten>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>The Momcozy AutoMeal Baby Food Maker steams, blends and self-cleans in one machine, and it’s on sale for $100 on Amazon. Here’s why parents like it.</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/select/shopping/momcozy-baby-food-maker-deal-of-the-day-rcna609283</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/select/shopping/momcozy-baby-food-maker-deal-of-the-day-rcna609283</link><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261112-dotd-momcozy-baby-food-maker-lf-main-9c6839.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1200\" width=\"2400\"><media:credit>Amazon</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">This baby food maker steams, blends and cleans itself with a touch of a button. </media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">This baby food maker steams, blends and cleans itself with a touch of a button. </media:description></media:content><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261112-dotd-momcozy-baby-food-maker-lf-sq-e749c0.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1200\" width=\"1200\"><media:credit>Amazon</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">This baby food maker steams, blends and cleans itself with a touch of a button. </media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">This baby food maker steams, blends and cleans itself with a touch of a button. </media:description></media:content><media:thumbnail url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2026-11/261112-dotd-momcozy-baby-food-maker-lf-main-9c6839.jpg\" height=\"1200\" width=\"2400\"></media:thumbnail><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><title>Calling all parents! This popular baby food maker is on sale for under $100</title><updateDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 GMT</updateDate></item><item><dc:creator>Mili Godio</dc:creator><dateTimeWritten>Mon, 11 Aug 2025 20:33:56 GMT</dateTimeWritten><description>We asked experts for the best meal delivery services in 2026. These are the best meal kit services for everyone from Blue Apron, Home Chef, CookUnity and more.</description><expires>2112-01-01T00:00:00.000+0000</expires><guid>https://www.nbcnews.com/select/shopping/best-meal-delivery-services-rcna224305</guid><link>https://www.nbcnews.com/select/shopping/best-meal-delivery-services-rcna224305</link><media:content url=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_fit_1500w/rockcms/2025-08/250807-meal-delivery-bd-main-4202d3.jpg\" type=\"image/jpeg\" medium=\"image\" height=\"1200\" width=\"2400\"><media:credit>Courtesy Zoe Malin</media:credit><media:text type=\"plain\">Our editors tried meal delivery services from popular brands like Blue Apron, Home Chef, Factor and CookUnity. Here&#39;s what we thought.</media:text><media:description type=\"plain\">Our editors tried meal delivery services from popular brands like Blue Apron, Home 